 Tw (place of refuge, but )Tj91 0 TD 2.295 Tw (as time progressed they saw in this region more and more a "national)Tj-91 -12 TD 4.41 Tw (home". Links between the Druze of Palestine and their brethren in Jebel Druze )Tj406 0 TD 0.69 Tc 0 Tw (had)Tj-406 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.768 Tw (strenghtened, and at the same time the Arabs of Palestine, whose policy )Tj341 0 TD 4.307 Tw (was to assimilate)Tj-341 -12 TD 4.398 Tw (minorities, especially Arab-speaking minorities, attempted )Tj284 0 TD 3.818 Tw (to have complete domination)Tj-284 -12 TD 0.13 Tc 0 Tw (over the Druze of Palestine. Epstein held )Tj188 0 TD 0 Tc 2.564 Tw (that although theoretically the Druze would be in)Tj-188 -12 TD 1.711 Tw (favour of transfer, he felt that in practice an argument )Tj257 0 TD 3.256 Tw (was likely to break out within the)Tj-257 -12 TD 0.617 Tw (Druze community - some would favour transfer whilst others would oppose )Tj348 0 TD 3.346 Tw (it. In order that)Tj-348 -12 TD 0.197 Tc 0 Tw (the transfer plan )Tj79 0 TD 0 Tc 1.276 Tw (be successful, Epstein wrote that a prior condition was strict secrecy. If any)Tj-79 -12 TD 0.967 Tw (word would get out prematurely, the Mufti would ensure that )Tj288 0 TD 1.126 Tw (an argument would break out)Tj-288 -12 TD 0.146 Tc 0 Tw (within the Druze community, thus preventing any possibility of the plan's realisation. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf398 3 TD (5)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-376 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.805 Tw (British authorities: Epstein considered that the British authorities would oppose )Tj383 0 TD 0.709 Tc 0 Tw (the)Tj-409 -12 TD 0.03 Tc (transfer of the Druze for the following reasons. During )Tj246 0 TD 0 Tc 1.508 Tw (the previous hundred years, the Druze)Tj-246 -12 TD 0.03 Tc 0 Tw (were one of the factors for the influence )Tj179 0 TD 0 Tc 2.536 Tw (of the British in Greater Syria. Since the first world)Tj-179 -12 TD 0.056 Tc 0 Tw (war, the Druze community in Palestine had served )Tj230 0 TD 0 Tc 1.812 Tw (as a link with the Druze living outsi