BT/F2 7 Tf181.5 781 TD 0.023 Tc 0 Tw (Chaim SIMONS : Proposals to Transfer Arabs from Palestine)Tj-10 -10 TD -0.18 Tc (\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321)Tj/F3 10 Tf-86 -25 TD 0 Tc (The Resolution of the British Common Wealth Party)Tj/F4 10 Tf26 -12 TD 0.114 Tc (The British Common Wealth Party, a Socialist splinter group, was founded in 1942 )Tj376 0 TD 0.667 Tc (with)Tj-402 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.838 Tw (a policy based on Christian morality and not Marxian scientific socialism. Prior to the )Tj405 0 TD 0 Tw (1945)Tj-405 -12 TD 5.266 Tw (General Election, there )Tj119 0 TD 5.941 Tw (were three Common Wealth members sitting in the British)Tj-119 -12 TD 0.156 Tc 0 Tw (Parliament. In 1945, the Party published a report on international affairs, containing a )Tj394 0 TD 0 Tc (section)Tj-394 -12 TD 4.59 Tw (on Palestine, which while )Tj134 0 TD 5.368 Tw (extremely sympathetic to Jewish aspirations, included two)Tj-134 -12 TD 0.111 Tc 0 Tw (sentences advocating partition of Palestine. At their Conference held in Liverpool in )Tj383 0 TD 0 Tc 3.128 Tw (1945, the)Tj-383 -12 TD -0.134 Tc 0 Tw (Hendon branch )Tj70 0 TD 0 Tc 1.554 Tw (of the Party submitted an amendment deleting the reference to partition and)Tj-70 -12 TD 0.174 Tc 0 Tw (inserting a more positive attitude towards the Jewish State, )Tj274 0 TD 0 Tc 2.019 Tw (which was then accepted by the)Tj-274 -12 TD 0.269 Tc 0 Tw (National Committee.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc (Included in the resolution )Tj117 0 TD 1.965 Tw (passed by the Conference was a paragraph dealing with the)Tj-143 -12 TD 0.058 Tc 0 Tw (transfer of Arabs from Palestine. "We do not favour )Tj233 0 TD 0 Tc 1.396 Tw (the principle of compulsory emigration in)Tj-233 -12 TD 1.984 Tw (any part of the world but we recommend that an )Tj238 0 TD 3.754 Tw (international commission be appointed,)Tj-238 -12 TD 1.641 Tw (including both Jewish and Arab representatives, )Tj226 0 TD 2.378 Tw (whose task shall be to draw up a scheme)Tj-226 -12 TD 4.377 Tw (involving as little displacement of the )Tj195 0 TD 4.216 Tw (Arab population as possible and arranging for)Tj-195 -12 TD 0.155 Tc 0 Tw (facilities for such Arab transfer as is necessary to adjacent territory." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf317 3 TD (1)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-295 -12 TD 0 Tc (It appears from the wording of )Tj140 0 TD 2.104 Tw (this resolution that "such Arab transfer as is necessary")Tj-166 -12 TD 4.014 Tw (might be a compulsory transfer. )Tj164 0 TD 4.969 Tw (Hence although opposed in principle to compulsory)Tj-164 -12 TD 4.143 Tw (emigration, the Party would have )Tj172 0 TD 5.279 Tw (appeared to have recognised that the situation in)Tj-172 -12 TD 0.059 Tc 0 Tw (Palestine was such as to necessitate extreme measures.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.521 Tw (In the July 1945 General Election, the )Tj183 0 TD 3.811 Tw (Common Wealth Party lost two of its three)Tj-209 -12 TD 0.198 Tc 0 Tw (Parliamentary seats. It failed to contest any further elections.)TjET0.24 w 85.12 121.88 m 228.12 121.88 l S 1 w BT/F4 7 Tf85.5 109 TD (1)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0 Tc 1.382 Tw ( / "Common Wealth Party Conference Support Jewish State", The Jewish Standard, \(London\), sixth year )Tj390 0 TD 1.977 Tw (no.1, 13)Tj-394 -9 TD 0.026 Tc 0 Tw (April 1945, p.2; "Common Wealth Attitude on Palestine", The Jewish Chronicle, \(London\), 13 April 1945, p.8.)Tj/F5 7 Tf176 -31 TD 0.269 Tc (\321    277    \321)TjET
