 Tw (Movement therefore has no interest whatsoever in )Tj229 0 TD 0 Tc 1.876 Tw (proposing a policy of transfer, neither has)Tj-229 -12 TD 1.68 Tw (it an interest in depriving the Arab people )Tj202 0 TD 4.274 Tw (of their natural and political aspirations." He)Tj-202 -12 TD 8.407 Tw (then explained the Hashomer Hazair scheme )Tj252 0 TD 11.687 Tw (for a Bi-National \(Jewish-Arab\))Tj-252 -12 TD 0.223 Tc 0 Tw (administration in Palestine. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf134 3 TD (1)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-112 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.405 Tw (A correspondent replying to this letter pointed )Tj219 0 TD 3.781 Tw (out that the majority of the Socialist)Tj-245 -12 TD 0.97 Tw (Zionist Movement members disapproved of the )Tj220 0 TD 3.655 Tw (bi-national idea and that Ben Israel spoke)Tj-220 -12 TD 0.117 Tc 0 Tw (only for Hashomer Hazair, a group which had polled about )Tj273 0 TD 0 Tc 2.479 Tw (one-fifth of the votes in the last)Tj-273 -12 TD 0 Tw (elections to the Conference )Tj122 0 TD 2.124 Tw (of the Jewish Labour Federation in Palestine. With regard to the)Tj-122 -12 TD 1.637 Tw (transfer question he continued, "Zionism, it is true, always believed )Tj317 0 TD 4.796 Tw (and still believes that)Tj-317 -12 TD 1.988 Tw (the Jewish Homeland )Tj104 0 TD 2.532 Tw (can be rebuilt without displacing or transferring a single Arab. The)Tj-104 -12 TD 1.356 Tw (Labour Party Executive, wisely, did not urge transfer as indispensable )Tj326 0 TD 2.003 Tw (and did not speak of)Tj-326 -12 TD 0 Tw (compulsion." The writer then quoted )Tj166 0 TD 1.716 Tw (from the text of the Labour Party Resolution, indicating)Tj-166 -12 TD 0.853 Tw (that the proposed transfer was "on human grounds and to )Tj268 0 TD 3.309 Tw (promote a stable settlement." He)Tj-268 -12 TD 2.425 Tw (concluded that one was no )Tj133 0 TD 4.855 Tw (worse a Socialist for believing in utilising the solution of)Tj-133 -12 TD 0.063 Tc 0 Tw (population transfer "as a cure for some thorny national problems." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf303 3 TD (2)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-281 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.828 Tw (Another correspondent, Baruch Ben Shalom, was critical )Tj272 0 TD 3.269 Tw (of those who opposed the)Tj-298 -12 TD 0.129 Tc 0 Tw (transfer )Tj38 0 TD 0 Tc 1.716 Tw (of Arabs pointing out that nearly half of the Arabs in Palestine had come from the)Tj-38 -12 TD 2.596 Tw (surrounding Arab countries during the course of the past twenty years )Tj344 0 TD 4.393 Tw (in order to take)Tj-344 -12 TD 0.231 Tc 0 Tw (advantage )Tj51 0 TD 0 Tc 2.145 Tw (of the ever-expanding industrial and agricultural opportunities in Palestine. Ben)Tj-51 -12 TD 4.192 Tw (Shalom then asked, "Could not similar industrial and agricultural )Tj330 0 TD 4.46 Tw (expansions in these)Tj-330 -12 TD 2.137 Tw (undeveloped but potentially rich and fertile )Tj209 0 TD 2.2 Tw (countries 'encourage' the Arabs to emigrate to)Tj-209 -12 TD 3.274 Tw (them from Palestine? Is there anything reactionary )Tj249 0 TD 2.785 Tw (in such a suggestion? Only a touchy)Tj-249 -12 TD 0.186 Tc 0 Tw (mentality would think so." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf129 3 TD (3)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-107 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.18 Tw (Probably the most vehemently pro-transfer letter )Tj232 0 TD 2.368 Tw (printed in the "Tribune" came from)Tj-258 -12 TD 0.152 Tc 0 Tw (Frederick Jellinek who wrote, "A )Tj152 0 TD 0 Tc 1.461 Tw (rejection in principle of 'voluntary transfer' of Arabs would)Tj-152 -12 TD 0.028 Tc 0 Tw (in practice amount to a sort of prohibition of )Tj200 0 TD 0 Tc 2.374 Tw (emigration. Apart from the fact that this would)Tj-200 -12 TD 0.075 Tc 0 Tw (constitute an undue restriction of civil rights, it )Tj214 0 TD 0 Tc 0.61 Tw (would be absurd if Jewish bodies would resort)Tj-214 -12 TD 2.225 Tw (to such a policy." Jellinek felt that since the )Tj211 0 TD 3.178 Tw (public associated transfer of population with)Tj-211 -12 TD 2.587 Tw (force, the expression "voluntary transfer" was open to misrepresentation. He )Tj366 0 TD 6.114 Tw (said that it)Tj-3