as Shertok's public pronouncement on the )Tj217 0 TD 0 Tc 1.059 Tw (question of transfer. However, to closed)Tj-243 -12 TD 0 Tw (sessions of the Jewish Agency Executive )Tj180 0 TD 2.103 Tw (and the Mapai Central Committee, both held only a)Tj-180 -12 TD 0.124 Tc 0 Tw (week before the appearance of the J.T.A. )Tj186 0 TD 0 Tc 2.325 Tw (news report, Shertok voiced rather different views,)Tj-186 -12 TD 0.114 Tc 0 Tw (when reporting on a meeting held with Philip Noel-Baker in London.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.399 Tc (Noel-Baker, )Tj60 0 TD 0 Tc 1.571 Tw (a member of the National Executive Committee of the Labour Party \(and)Tj-86 -12 TD 1.537 Tw (at a future date a )Tj85 0 TD 3.334 Tw (recipient of the Nobel Prize for Peace\) had asked Shertok, "Why is it)Tj-85 -12 TD 0.047 Tc 0 Tw (impossible to transfer Arabs from Palestine? We will give them one hundred million pounds )Tj416 0 TD 0 Tc (to)Tj-416 -12 TD 0.316 Tc (settle elsewhere." Shertok )Tj124 0 TD 0 Tc 3.271 Tw (reported that he had explained that although this resettlement)Tj-124 -12 TD 0.098 Tc 0 Tw ("might be possible in the final stages," transfer should not be advocated as a prior condition )Tj416 0 TD 0 Tc (to)Tj-416 -12 TD 0.193 Tc (solving the Middle East dilemma. If the )Tj185 0 TD 0 Tc 1.96 Tw (overall solution were to be linked with the transfer)Tj-185 -12 TD 1.328 Tw (of the Arabs, this transfer would be regarded as an )Tj240 0 TD 3.092 Tw (indispensable condition for settling the)Tj-240 -12 TD 2.87 Tw (Palestine problem. This might result in the suggestion that without )Tj327 0 TD 4.066 Tw (transfer of Arabs, it)Tj-327 -12 TD -0.027 Tc 0 Tw (would be impossible to absorb further Jews in the country. As a transfer of )Tj330 0 TD 0 Tc 0.627 Tw (Arabs would be very)Tj-330 -12 TD 0.306 Tc 0 Tw (difficult, "as difficult as dividing the Red Sea," it )Tj231 0 TD 0 Tc 2.025 Tw (would be easy for the British to arrive at)Tj-231 -12 TD 0.046 Tc 0 Tw (the conclusion that Palestine could not absor