ement that no measures of compulsion will be)Tj-67 -12 TD -0.099 Tc 0 Tw (used under any circumstances." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf143 3 TD (1)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 0.124 Tc (\) [As we have already seen, )Tj127 0 TD 0 Tc 1.573 Tw (to a \322different audience,\323 Locker)Tj-274 -12 TD 0.103 Tc 0 Tw (described the transfer as \322a very just idea.\323])Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.881 Tw (Misrepresentation was )Tj109 0 TD 2.714 Tw (not limited to outsiders and even a few Labour Members of)Tj-135 -12 TD 0.144 Tc 0 Tw (Parliament joined in the attack. One of these was )Tj225 0 TD 0 Tc 1.311 Tw (Richard Stokes, a member who managed to)Tj-225 -12 TD 0.103 Tc 0 Tw (combine extreme pacifism and internationalism, with )Tj244 0 TD 0 Tc 3.012 Tw (a barely-concealed anti-Jewish bias. In)Tj-244 -12 TD 0.192 Tc 0 Tw (a pamphlet entitled "Labour and the )Tj170 0 TD 0 Tc 2.928 Tw (Post-War Settlement", Stokes wondered why Palestine)Tj-170 -12 TD 0.393 Tc 0 Tw (had )Tj21 0 TD 0 Tc 1.911 Tw ("found such a prominent place in the Party policy." He felt that the policy outlined in)Tj-21 -12 TD 0.134 Tc 0 Tw (the pamphlet was a contradiction of the principles enunciated for the benefit )Tj351 0 TD 0 Tc 0.821 Tw (of the occupants)Tj-351 -12 TD 0.144 Tc 0 Tw (of the Colonial Empire. "Zionism is a )Tj171 0 TD 0 Tc 1.239 Tw (controversial matter even amongst the Jews," continued)Tj-171 -12 TD 0.219 Tc 0 Tw (Stokes, "Is )Tj50 0 TD 0 Tc 1.452 Tw (the Labour Party as a whole to be committed to being pro-Zionist and anti-Arab.)Tj-50 -12 TD 0.084 Tc 0 Tw (The suggestion that the Arabs should )Tj171 0 TD 0 Tc 1.171 Tw (be cleared out of Palestine is a dangerous one, and will)Tj-171 -12 TD 1.715 Tw (be resisted by the teeming millions of India and the Middle East." )Tj312 0 TD 2.794 Tw (The introduction to this)Tj-312 -12 TD 0 Tw (document stated )Tj77 0 TD 2.61 Tw (that the Parliamentary Peace Aims Group, a group of exclusively Labour)Tj-77 -12 TD 0 Tw (members of the Lords and Commons, was re