l by the Government,)Tj-296 -12 TD 1.032 Tw (some weeks before D-day, to avoid mass )Tj190 0 TD 4.121 Tw (travelling. The Conference was finally held that)Tj-190 -12 TD 0 Tw (December.)Tj/F3 10 Tf0 -24 TD (The Attitude of Clement Attlee to Transfer)Tj/F4 10 Tf26 -12 TD 0.173 Tc (The leader of )Tj63 0 TD 0 Tc 2.607 Tw (the British Labour Party at that period was Clement Attlee. What was)Tj-89 -12 TD 0.178 Tc 0 Tw (his attitude to the transfer of Arabs from Palestine?)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc (As )Tj14 0 TD 1.412 Tw (previously described, in November 1939 a meeting had taken place at the House of)Tj-40 -12 TD 0 Tw (Commons between Major Attlee, Tom Williams, Weizmann and )Tj287 0 TD 2.973 Tw (other Zionist leaders. At this)Tj-287 -12 TD 0.071 Tc 0 Tw (meeting, Weizmann put the Zionist )Tj162 0 TD 0 Tc 1.915 Tw (case and taking the Peel Report as his starting point, he)Tj-162 -12 TD 0 Tw (spoke )Tj29 0 TD 2.768 Tw (of the idea of a Jewish State and the transfer of population. "We must have some)Tj-29 -12 TD 2.922 Tw (territorial basis there, and )Tj128 0 TD 2.661 Tw (that would mean an improved Peel scheme, possibly Palestine)Tj-128 -12 TD 0.141 Tc 0 Tw (west of the Jordan, with some transfer of a part at least of the Arab population.")Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.387 Tw (The notes on the conversation, which were written by Moshe Shertok )Tj324 0 TD 1.553 Tw (continue, "Major)Tj-350 -12 TD 0.04 Tc 0 Tw (Attlee nodded assent when transfer of population was mentioned. He added however. )Tj389 0 TD 0 Tc (Are you)Tj-389 -12 TD 0.476 Tw (not putting all your eggs in one )Tj145 0 TD 3.507 Tw (basket? There are after all, other baskets." To this Locker)Tj-145 -12 TD 0.205 Tc 0 Tw (replied that the Zionists only had one basket. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf215 3 TD (3)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-193 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.731 Tw (Commenting on this meeting, Gorny in his book "The )Tj255 0 TD 3.412 Tw (British Labour Movement and)Tj-281 -12 TD 4.66 Tw (Zionism" noted that Shertok mentioned no similar assent by Attlee when )Tj376 0 TD 0 Tw (Weizmann)Tj-376 -12 TD 1.696 Tw (mentioned a Jewish State. Here Gorny suggested that "Attlee was, of )Tj324 0 TD 1.308 Tw (course opposed to the)Tj-324 -12 TD 0.139 Tc 0 Tw (concept of a Jewish State, but may have believed that transfer of population )Tj347 0 TD 0 Tc 2.025 Tw (would create the)Tj-347 -12 TD 0.291 Tc 0 Tw (possibility of a political entity shared )Tj178 0 TD 0 Tc 1.72 Tw (by the two peoples living in Palestine." Gorny added)Tj-178 -12 TD 5.371 Tw (that international )Tj90 0 TD 3.833 Tw (experience had shown that transfer of population was linked to the)Tj-90 -12 TD 0.228 Tc 0 Tw (establishment of separate national states. )Tj193 0 TD 0 Tc 2.308 Tw (He suggested that "if Attlee did, in fact, approve)Tj-193 -12 TD 0.253 Tc 0 Tw (of the idea )Tj52 0 TD 0 Tc 1.471 Tw (of population transfer, he was recognizing something which he had never before)Tj-52 -12 TD 0.179 Tc 0 Tw (admitted, namely that there was a connection between the Jewish plight and Palestine." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf408 3 TD (4)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-386 -12 TD 0.282 Tc (Harold Wilson, a later leader )Tj139 0 TD 0 Tc 1.767 Tw (of the Labour Party and British Prime Minister between)Tj-165 -12 TD 0.056 Tc 0 Tw (the years 1964-70 and 1974-6, made a far less cautious assessment of Attlee's views on )Tj385 0 TD 0 Tc 3.071 Tw (a Jewish)Tj-385 -12 TD 0.49 Tc 0 Tw (State )Tj27 0 TD 0 Tc 1.88 Tw (and population transfer. "Attlee was, in fact, fully committed to an independent state)Tj-27 -12 TD 0.102 Tc 0 Tw (for the Jews in Palestine - )Tj117 0 TD 0 Tc 1.697 Tw (even to the extent of expelling some of the Arabs." He added that)Tj-117 -12 TD 0.133 Tc 0 Tw (Attlee as the Party Leader was one one of the principal signatories )Tj304 0 TD 0 Tc 3.009 Tw (of the National Executive)Tj-304 -12 TD 0.139 Tc 0 Tw (Committee's Annual Report of 1944 which included this Palestine paragraph. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf358 3 TD (5)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 