raphy, that he and his colleagues)Tj-190 -12 TD 0.152 Tc 0 Tw (had constantly pressed their case and that in )Tj206 0 TD 0 Tc 1.02 Tw (1943 and 1944, he had discussed the question of)Tj-206 -12 TD 0.111 Tc 0 Tw (the Jewish National Home with some of the leading members of the Labour Party. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf378 3 TD (3)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-356 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.276 Tw (In the spring of 1944, Shertok had been )Tj193 0 TD 3.414 Tw (in England. On his return to Palestine, he)Tj-219 -12 TD 2.31 Tw (reported to the Jewish Agency Executive and on the following day to the )Tj354 0 TD 7.299 Tw (Mapai Central)Tj-354 -12 TD 2.025 Tw (Committee. He told these bodies that )Tj179 0 TD 1.756 Tw (one of the new phenomena which he encountered in)Tj-179 -12 TD 0 Tw (England was an enthusiasm for )Tj141 0 TD 1.807 Tw (population transfer, not as a result of Jewish initiative but of)Tj-141 -12 TD 1.516 Tw (non-Jewish logic. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf85 3 TD (4)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 1.522 Tw (\) The Labour Party had )Tj113 0 TD 2.992 Tw (concluded that there were two possibilities for)Tj-202 -12 TD 1.241 Tw (Palestine - to do nothing or to give it to the Jews. In the latter case one would )Tj364 0 TD 3.554 Tw (have to give)Tj-364 -12 TD 3.318 Tw (them the entire country "and thus it will be necessary to remove )Tj325 0 TD 7.163 Tw (the Arabs." Shertok)Tj-325 -12 TD 3.91 Tw (explained that reports of this reasoning had reached the Zionists from various )Tj394 0 TD -0.306 Tc 0 Tw (sources)Tj-394 -12 TD 0.225 Tc (including Dalton and Philip Noel-Baker. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf194 3 TD (5)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-172 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.583 Tw (Shertok then reported to both the Jewish Agency Executive and the )Tj328 0 TD 7.299 Tw (Mapai Central)Tj-354 -12 TD 1.571 Tw (Committee that a member of the British Government who was proficient )Tj341 0 TD 4.095 Tw (in foreign affairs,)Tj-341 -12 TD 0 Tw (and was considered to be a candidate for Foreign Minister was given )Tj307 0 TD 2.139 Tw (the task of compiling the)Tj-307 -12 TD 0 Tw (section )Tj33 0 TD 2.059 Tw (of the Party's annual report which dealt with foreign affairs. It was the work of an)Tj-33 -12 TD 0.286 Tc 0 Tw (individual )Tj52 0 TD 0 Tc 1.859 Tw (and "without anyone putting the idea in his head, he inserted at the end of the)Tj-52 -12 TD 0.157 Tc 0 Tw (section on foreign affairs the paragraph on Palestine." )Tj248 0 TD 0 Tc 2.442 Tw (Shertok said that according to Dalton)Tj-248 -12 TD 0.278 Tc 0 Tw (the British Labour Party had had )Tj157 0 TD 0 Tc 2.136 Tw (a fixed and standard policy on Palestine which obligated)Tj-157 -12 TD 1.993 Tw (the establishment of a Jewish National Home in accordance with )Tj308 0 TD 5.78 Tw (the Balfour Declaration,)Tj-308 -12 TD 0.106 Tc 0 Tw (but had never had the boldness to think out the logical )Tj250 0 TD 0 Tc 1.324 Tw (conclusions from this policy. The time)Tj-250 -12 TD 0.027 Tc 0 Tw (had come to follow these conclusions to a logical )Tj219 0 TD 0 Tc 1.737 Tw (end, namely that Palestine must be a Jewish)Tj-219 -12 TD 2.479 Tw (State. If it is )Tj64 0 TD 2.407 Tw ("too small to meet the requirements of the Jewish people, we must think of)Tj-64 -12 TD 0.472 Tw (changing its borders by means )Tj140 0 TD 1.832 Tw (of annexing areas from the surrounding states. We must also)Tj-140 -12 TD 1.202 Tw (discuss the question of transferring the Arabs from Palestine to )Tj293 0 TD 1.351 Tw (other countries and we must)Tj-293 -12 TD 2.501 Tw (also speak of )Tj67 0 TD 5.389 Tw (allotting additional territory in north Africa." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf237 3 TD (6)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 4.252 Tw (\) To the Mapai Central)Tj-308 -12 TD 3.595 Tw (Committee, Shertok )Tj98 0 TD 3.646 Tw (added, "With regard to transfer, we had very serious doubts... not)Tj-98 -12 TD 0.154 Tc 0 Tw (necessarily )Tj53 0 TD 0 Tc 1.892 Tw (aroused by the content of this paragraph." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf205 3 TD (7)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 2.631 Tw (\) However, we shall see later that)Tj-262 