her problems )Tj187 0 TD 4.454 Tw (which would need verifying, such as land)Tj-213 -12 TD 0.03 Tc 0 Tw (ownership, size of rural and urban populations, and social classes )Tj295 0 TD 0 Tc 1.442 Tw (among the Arab population.)Tj-295 -12 TD 3.524 Tw (Towards the end of the meeting, Nachmani proposed investigating )Tj331 0 TD 7.01 Tw (the possibilities of)Tj-331 -12 TD 1.561 Tw (settlement in Syria and Transjordan. Ben-Ami was against transferring Arabs to )Tj372 0 TD 0 Tw (Transjordan)Tj-372 -12 TD 0.209 Tc (as he required that this area be )Tj145 0 TD 0 Tc 1.829 Tw (left empty for future Jewish settlement. However, he agreed)Tj-145 -12 TD 2.523 Tw (that in the case of absolute necessity, the Arabs could be settled in )Tj326 0 TD 3.749 Tw (the southern part of)Tj-326 -12 TD 0.829 Tw (Transjordan. The meeting )Tj119 0 TD 3.508 Tw (resolved that within a fortnight, Nachmani and Epstein should)Tj-119 -12 TD 0.198 Tc 0 Tw (present material on the possibilities )Tj167 0 TD 0 Tc 2.135 Tw (of settlement in Syria and Transjordan, after which the)Tj-167 -12 TD 0.091 Tc 0 Tw (Committee would make a general inspection of the various sites in Syria. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf335 3 TD (3)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))TjET0.24 w 85.12 132.88 m 228.12 132.88 l S 1 w BT/F4 7 Tf85.5 120 TD (1)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.016 Tc ( / Minutes, Sub-Committee on Transfer of Arabs, 1 & 5 December 1937, pp.1-2, \(CZA S25/10060\).)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (2)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0 Tc ( / Ibid., p.3.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (3)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 2.315 Tw ( / Minutes, )Tj49 0 TD 3.359 Tw (Population Transfer Committee, Sub-Committee on Settlement, 5 December 1937, pp.1-2, \(CZA)Tj/F5 7 Tf123 -31 TD 0.269 Tc 0 Tw (\321    232    \321)TjET
