w (period, otherwise the transfer would be offset by natural)Tj-137 -12 TD 0.096 Tc 0 Tw (population growth.)Tj26 -12 TD (After very briefly discussing the methods )Tj190 0 TD 0 Tc 1.619 Tw (of resettlement in the Balkans, he went on to)Tj-216 -12 TD 2.259 Tw (explain the special requirements regarding Palestine, namely: the )Tj309 0 TD 3.297 Tw (order in which different)Tj-309 -12 TD 2.231 Tw (classes of Arabs should be transferred; the development of Transjordan for the )Tj376 0 TD 1.222 Tw (purpose of)Tj-376 -12 TD 3.168 Tw (resettlement; the special arrangements for the transfer )Tj263 0 TD 3.4 Tw (of Druze villages from the upper)Tj-263 -12 TD 0.149 Tc 0 Tw (Galilee to Syria and Lebanon; and the moral responsibility towards the Arab transferees.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc (Mendelsohn concluded his lecture on a comment regarding the financial )Tj322 0 TD 1.069 Tw (aspects of such a)Tj-348 -12 TD 0.212 Tc 0 Tw (transfer. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf45 3 TD (3)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-23 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.628 Tw (Following the lecture, various other speakers briefly mentioned a few of )Tj350 0 TD 4.928 Tw (the points)Tj-376 -12 TD 0 Tw (discussed by Mendelsohn in his lecture. These included agrarian reform and the question of )Tj409 0 TD 0.709 Tc (the)Tj-409 -12 TD 0.077 Tc (transfer of other minority groups such as the Druze and the Christians. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf325 3 TD (4)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-303 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.878 Tw (In a letter written )Tj87 0 TD 2.828 Tw (on the following day by Thon to the Political Department of the)Tj-113 -12 TD 0.045 Tc 0 Tw (Jewish Agency, he pointed out that "one of the foremost and decisive conditions )Tj360 0 TD 0 Tc (for the success)Tj-360 -12 TD 0.155 Tc (of the proposed Jewish State is the transfer )Tj198 0 TD 0 Tc 1.849 Tw (of the Arab population from its area." Thon said)Tj-198 -12 TD 0 Tw (that public opinion in Europe and America and amongst the )Tj269 0 TD 0.694 Tw (Diaspora Jews could be influenced)Tj-269 -12 TD 5.016