 Joseph Weitz, Director of the Jewish National Fund's )Tj336 0 TD 3.414 Tw (Land Development)Tj-336 -12 TD 1.214 Tw (Division; Dr. Alfred Bonne, an economist )Tj192 0 TD 2.725 Tw (who had directed the Economic Archives for the)Tj-192 -12 TD 1.703 Tw (Near East in )Tj62 0 TD 2.843 Tw (Jerusalem; and Joseph Nachami, Director of the Jewish National Fund Land)Tj-62 -12 TD 0.291 Tc 0 Tw (Office for the Galilee area. Eliahu Epstein \(later Elath\), Director of )Tj313 0 TD 0 Tc 2.602 Tw (the Middle East Section)Tj-313 -12 TD 0.172 Tc 0 Tw (of the Jewish Agency's Political Department acted as secretary. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf294 3 TD (2)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-272 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.263 Tw (The Population Transfer Committee held its first meeting on 15 November 1937. )Tj384 0 TD 0 Tw (Dr.)Tj-410 -12 TD 1.852 Tw (Joseph )Tj34 0 TD 3.461 Tw (opened the meeting and told its members that their function was to "prepare a)Tj-34 -12 TD 0.041 Tc 0 Tw (programme for the transfer of population and to coordinate the information )Tj341 0 TD 0 Tc 2.845 Tw (required for this.")Tj-341 -12 TD 0.082 Tc 0 Tw (Their foremost task was to )Tj122 0 TD 0 Tc 1.832 Tw (assemble comprehensive details on the Arab population dwelling)Tj-122 -12 TD 0.201 Tc 0 Tw (in the area designated as the future Jewish State.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.097 Tw (Weitz asked whether the Committee was to )Tj210 0 TD 1.95 Tw (express its opinion on the expediency of)Tj-236 -12 TD 5.514 Tw (existing possibilities )Tj103 0 TD 4.46 Tw (for the transfer of the Arab population, or just to assemble the)Tj-103 -12 TD 4.954 Tw (information. Thon answered that the )Tj190 0 TD 5.456 Tw (Committee must first assemble and digest the)Tj-190 -12 TD 0.037 Tc 0 Tw (information. Only then would it be possible to discuss Weitz's question.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.106 Tc (Granovsky wanted the Committee to examine the possibility of granting the )Tj347 0 TD 0 Tc (Arabs some)Tj-373 -12 TD 1.073 Tw (favour in exchange for any concessions they might make to the Jews. He was )Tj357 0 TD 0 Tw (very concerned)Tj-357 -12 TD 0.218 Tc (with the mechanics of transfer and felt that )Tj202 0 TD 0 Tc 1.766 Tw (the Committee should discuss "how the transfer)Tj-202 -12 TD 0.132 Tc 0 Tw (of population will be carried out" and "by what means the transfer will be implemented.")Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 4.325 Tw (Thon said that the )Tj100 0 TD 5.135 Tw (activities of the Committee should be divided between the)Tj-126 -12 TD 0.756 Tw (assembling information concerning the Arab )Tj204 0 TD 3.038 Tw (population, and investigating opportunities for)Tj-204 -12 TD 1.554 Tw (agriculture in Transjordan. This, said )Tj174 0 TD 2.439 Tw (Thon, was the only way to solve the problem of the)Tj-174 -12 TD 2.847 Tw (transfer of the Arabs living within the borders )Tj229 0 TD 4.037 Tw (of the proposed Jewish State. [The Peel)Tj-229 -12 TD 2.653 Tw (Commission had also called for an investigation to determine the )Tj317 0 TD 5.394 Tw (absorptive capacity of)Tj-317 -12 TD 0 Tw (Transjordan.])Tj26 -12 TD 2.589 Tw (Nachmani said that the Committee "needs to find a solution to the question of )Tj383 0 TD 0.709 Tc 0 Tw (the)Tj-409 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.491 Tw (means of transfer. This forces us to deal not only with the details )Tj307 0 TD 0.974 Tw (and minutae concerning a)Tj-307 -12 TD 1.297 Tw (plan for the removal of the residents but also to concern ourselves with the )Tj351 0 TD 6.441 Tw (possibilities for)Tj-351 -12 TD 0.298 Tc 0 Tw (their resettlement elsewhere.")Tj26 -12 TD 0.18 Tc (Weitz disagreed. He felt that the Committee's first consideration should be )Tj346 0 TD 0 Tc 1.4 Tw (how to free)Tj-372 -12 TD 0.632 Tw (more land for )Tj65 0 TD 2.593 Tw (Jewish settlement in areas of Arab concentration "and what is the optimum)Tj-65 -12 TD 0.123 Tc 0 Tw (solution for the removal of the Arab residents from these areas.")Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.669 Tw (Joseph explained that )Tj106 0 TD 2.074 Tw (coordinating information was only one of the functions of this)Tj-132 -12 TD 2.669 Tw (Committee. It would have to deal )Tj167 0 TD 3.1 Tw (with a number of other problems connected with the)Tj-167 -12 TD 2.737 Tw (transfer, in the light of experience from other population )Tj277 0 TD 3.552 Tw (transfers. The members of this)Tj-277 -12 TD 0.185 Tc 0 Tw (Committee would have to familiarise )Tj174 0 TD 0 Tc 2.238 Tw (themselves with all aspects of transfer as they would)Tj-174 -12 TD 0 Tw (be the Jewish Agency experts on all questions connected with population )Tj326 0 TD 2.229 Tw (transfer. The meeting)Tj-326 -12 TD -0.037 Tc 0 Tw (ended with a discussion on nomination of further )Tj220 0 TD 0 Tc 1.391 Tw (members to the Committee and allocation of)Tj-220 -12 TD -0.062 Tc 0 Tw (duties among the members. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf127 3 TD (3)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))TjET0.24 w 85.12 132.88 m 228.12 132.88 l S 1 w BT/F4 7 Tf85.5 120 TD (1)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.039 Tc ( / Notes on Conference, 25 October 1937, \(CZA S25/10109\).)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (2)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.033 Tc ( / Minutes, J. A. Exec., vol 27/1, no.14, 21 November 1937, p.3, \(CZA\).)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (3)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.029 Tc ( / Minutes, Population Transfer Committee, 15 November 1937, \(CZA S25/10060\).)Tj/F5 7 Tf172 -31 TD 0.269 Tc (\321    229    \321)TjET
