ge of the Greek and Turkish statesmen had been )Tj304 0 TD 4.451 Tw (justified by the resultant)Tj-304 -12 TD 0.053 Tc 0 Tw (cordial relations between these two countries. On this Ormsby-Gore asked, )Tj338 0 TD 0 Tc 1.681 Tw ("The question was:)Tj-338 -12 TD 0.055 Tc 0 Tw (Were responsible statesmen justified in taking not )Tj226 0 TD 0 Tc 1.935 Tw (a pessimistic view, not the most optimistic)Tj-226 -12 TD 0.21 Tc 0 Tw (view, but a reasonably optimistic view?" He maintained that they were. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf337 3 TD (4)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-315 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.317 Tw (Towards the end of the proceedings, this )Tj192 0 TD 3.026 Tw (comparison with the Greco-Turkish transfer)Tj-218 -12 TD 0 Tw (came up again in a reply given )Tj139 0 TD 1.297 Tw (by Ormsby-Gore to a written question. He considered that the)Tj-139 -12 TD 2.02 Tw (problem )Tj42 0 TD 4.815 Tw (of the Arab transfer was easier even than the Greco-Turkish interchange of)Tj-42 -12 TD -0.031 Tc 0 Tw (population, since the Arabs would be moving only a )Tj233 0 TD 0 Tc 1.966 Tw (short distance to a society with the same)TjET0.24 w 85.12 142.88 m 228.12 142.88 l S 1 w BT/F4 7 Tf85.5 130 TD (1)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.098 Tc 0 Tw ( / PMC Minutes, p.22.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (2)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0 Tc ( / Ibid., p.26.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (3)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD ( / Ibid., p.177.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (4)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD ( / Ibid., p.40.)Tj/F5 7 Tf172 -31 TD 0.269 Tc (\321    216    \321)TjET
