hild felt that a small Jewish State would not )Tj336 0 TD 2.681 Tw (solve the problems)Tj-336 -12 TD 1.364 Tw (since agitators from )Tj94 0 TD 2.887 Tw (the Arab State would foment yet more strife in the Jewish State. He)Tj-94 -12 TD 0.071 Tc 0 Tw (discounted the parallel of Greece and Turkey since there )Tj256 0 TD 0 Tc 1.589 Tw (the population to be transferred was)Tj-256 -12 TD 0.164 Tc 0 Tw (larger and the distances were greater than in Palestine.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 3.016 Tw (However, despite his "dislike" of "this idea", Rothschild did accept the principle )Tj390 0 TD 0 Tw (of)Tj-416 -12 TD 0.073 Tc (transfer, but with certain provisos. "The Commission envisage transfer to )Tj331 0 TD 0 Tc 2.451 Tw (the new Arab State,)Tj-331 -12 TD 0 Tw (but )Tj17 0 TD 2.438 Tw (there are greater opportunities in Trans-Jordan." [To be accurate, the Peel Commission)Tj-17 -12 TD 2.718 Tw (planned on transfer to all the areas )Tj175 0 TD 3.501 Tw (of the proposed Arab State \(including Transjordan\),)Tj-175 -12 TD 0.054 Tc 0 Tw (provided large-scale plans for immigration and development were executed]. )Tj349 0 TD 0 Tc 3.608 Tw ("With regard to)Tj-349 -12 TD 0.096 Tc 0 Tw (the urban population," )Tj105 0 TD 0 Tc 1.294 Tw (continued Rothschild, "there should be scope in the towns of the new)Tj-105 -12 TD 0.403 Tc 0 Tw (Arab State." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf64 3 TD (2)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 0 Tc (\) His prime aim here was to ensure )Tj158 0 TD 0.611 Tw (that urban Arabs were not forced to become)Tj-226 -12 TD 0.095 Tc 0 Tw (land labourers, a point also made later in the debate by Douglas Clifton Brown.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.284 Tw (The recommendation of the Peel Commission for the partition of )Tj301 0 TD 5.055 Tw (Palestine placed the)Tj-327 -12 TD 0.401 Tc 0 Tw (Galilee with its )Tj76 0 TD 0 Tc 2.324 Tw (almost wholly Arab population within the boundaries of the Jewish State.)Tj-76 -12 TD 0.069 Tc 0 Tw (The population transfer from this area was to be effected only on a 