t )Tj397 0 TD 0 Tc 2.897 Tw (in the)Tj-397 -12 TD 0.149 Tc 0 Tw (areas of Transjordan, the Jordan Valley and Beersheba.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 3.519 Tw (Support for the transfer )Tj121 0 TD 4.621 Tw (proposal was also voiced by Earl Edward Winterton, a)Tj-147 -12 TD 3.573 Tw (Conservative member of over thirty years standing, )Tj256 0 TD 5.223 Tw (who had served in Gallipoli and)Tj-256 -12 TD 0.174 Tc 0 Tw (Palestine during the First World War and was afterwards Under-Secretary of State )Tj381 0 TD 0 Tc 3.053 Tw (for India.)Tj-381 -12 TD 0.104 Tc 0 Tw (It is of interest to )Tj79 0 TD 0 Tc 2.047 Tw (note that although Winterton was an anti-Zionist and a leading supporter)Tj-79 -12 TD 0.097 Tc 0 Tw (of the Arabs, he supported the )Tj140 0 TD 0 Tc 1.92 Tw (population transfer proposal of the Peel Commission. Several)Tj-140 -12 TD 3.392 Tw (months earlier, Winterton had )Tj150 0 TD 3.934 Tw (suggested that Palestine be divided in such a way that)Tj-150 -12 TD 1.206 Tw (Western Palestine up to the Jordan would be a Jewish State and Transjordan )Tj355 0 TD 3.928 Tw (an Arab State.)Tj-355 -12 TD 1.151 Tw (This was conditional on the British Government's investing very large sums of money in )Tj409 0 TD 0.709 Tc 0 Tw (the)Tj-409 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.497 Tw (development of Transjordan and the Arabs in the Jewish State \(of )Tj308 0 TD 3.722 Tw (Western Palestine\) being)Tj-308 -12 TD -0.024 Tc 0 Tw (given the choice of remaining or moving to Transjordan. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf254 3 TD (3)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-232 -12 TD -0.069 Tc (In his speech to the House of Commons, )Tj178 0 TD 0 Tc 2.129 Tw (Winterton said "The question of transfer is still)Tj-204 -12 TD 0.167 Tc 0 Tw (in a very tentative state but I )Tj134 0 TD 0 Tc 1.139 Tw (should hope that no one on either side of the House would say)Tj-134 -12 TD 0.138 Tc 0 Tw (that the scheme is a bad one." He commended the "very satisfactory transfer )Tj349 0 TD 0 Tc 2.346 Tw (of minorities" in)Tj-349 -12 TD 0.097 Tc