ansferred, Wilson added)Tj-226 -12 TD 1.651 Tw (that the Jews should give the fullest assurances to the Arabs who )Tj309 0 TD 2.793 Tw (wished to remain in the)Tj-309 -12 TD 0.152 Tc 0 Tw (Jewish State. He believed that many Arabs would stay since nationalism had not reached )Tj409 0 TD 0.709 Tc (the)Tj-409 -12 TD 0.216 Tc (point where they would willingly leave their ancestral lands. )Tj285 0 TD 0 Tc 2.26 Tw (In a similar vein, Wilson said)Tj-285 -12 TD 0.214 Tc 0 Tw (that the Arabs should )Tj103 0 TD 0 Tc 1.495 Tw (give the fullest assurances to the many Jews who, he believed, would)Tj-103 -12 TD 0.218 Tc 0 Tw (wish to remain in the Arab State. He believed that "population )Tj292 0 TD 0 Tc 0.654 Tw (makes work and work makes)Tj-292 -12 TD 0.229 Tc 0 Tw (population" so that the )Tj109 0 TD 0 Tc 1.628 Tw (Jewish population in the area of the proposed Jewish State could be)Tj-109 -12 TD 0.113 Tc 0 Tw (considerably increased "without any great transference of population." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf326 3 TD (6)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))TjET0.24 w 85.12 162.88 m 228.12 162.88 l S 1 w BT/F4 7 Tf85.5 150 TD (1)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD -0.033 Tc ( / Lords, 20 July 1937, col.651.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (2)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0 Tc ( / Parliamentary Debates, Commons, vol.326, \(henceforth Commons\), 21 July 1937, col.2250.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (3)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD ( / Ben-Gurion, Memoirs, vol.4, op. cit., p.123.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (4)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD ( / Commons, 21 July 1937, col.2357.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (5)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD ( / Ibid., col.2294.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (6)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD ( / Ibid., col.2296.)Tj/F5 7 Tf172 -31 TD 0.269 Tc (\321    211    \321)TjET
