posed the compulsory Greco-Turkish population)Tj-105 -12 TD 0.19 Tc 0 Tw (transfer, he had been sharply )Tj137 0 TD 0 Tc 2.635 Tw (criticised for the "inhumanity of his proposal." However, the)Tj-137 -12 TD 1.921 Tw (Commission considered that )Tj135 0 TD 4.101 Tw (the success of the transfer had fully justified the apparent)Tj-135 -12 TD 0.393 Tc 0 Tw ("inhumanity.")Tj26 -12 TD 0.121 Tc (Samuel noted that another part of the report referred to the protection of )Tj332 0 TD 0 Tc 2.493 Tw (minorities and)Tj-358 -12 TD 2.97 Tw (asked whether the protection offered to )Tj195 0 TD 3.701 Tw (the Arab minority would take the form of the)Tj-195 -12 TD -0.207 Tc 0 Tw (compulsory uprooting )Tj98 0 TD 0 Tc 2.192 Tw (and relocation elsewhere. In fact, paragraph 39 of Chapter xxii of the)Tj-98 -12 TD 0.265 Tc 0 Tw (Peel Report states that the whole )Tj156 0 TD 0 Tc 1.347 Tw (purpose of the proposal for the transfer of population was)Tj-156 -12 TD 0.046 Tc 0 Tw (to protect minorities. The emergence of nationalism as a force )Tj277 0 TD 0 Tc 2.784 Tw (after the First World War, was)Tj-277 -12 TD -0.136 Tc 0 Tw (endangering )Tj57 0 TD 0 Tc 1.345 Tw (minorities in Europe and Asia including Palestine. However, Samuel questioned)Tj-57 -12 TD 0.165 Tc 0 Tw (whether it would be possible to relieve the large disparity between the size of the Jewish )Tj408 0 TD 0 Tc (and)Tj-408 -12 TD 3.887 Tw (Arab populations in "the so-called Jewish State" by means of )Tj308 0 TD 5.137 Tw (a transfer such as that)Tj-308 -12 TD 0.18 Tc 0 Tw (advocated in the Peel Report. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf141 3 TD (1)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-119 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.637 Tw (Lord Melchett, who was at )Tj134 0 TD 3.585 Tw (the time Chairman of the Jewish Agency Commission,)Tj-160 -12 TD -0.136 Tc 0 Tw (supported )Tj47 0 TD 0 Tc 2.679 Tw (the transfer of population. Unlike Samuel, Melchett accepted the parallel of the)Tj-47 -12 TD 0.112 Tc 0 Tw (Greco-Turkish transfer and added that he often )Tj217 0 