orts)Tj-404 -12 TD 0.155 Tc (of political solutions )Tj96 0 TD 0 Tc 1.847 Tw (regarding the Arab question and "I told myself: The historical solution)Tj-96 -12 TD 0.118 Tc 0 Tw (will be population )Tj86 0 TD 0 Tc 1.523 Tw (exchange." Katznelson knew that there were Arab countries neighbouring)Tj-86 -12 TD 0.938 Tw (Palestine who needed money and an increase )Tj210 0 TD 1.891 Tw (in population, but to speak about it would be)Tj-210 -12 TD 0.095 Tc 0 Tw (harmful and could lead to the )Tj137 0 TD 0 Tc 2.4 Tw (Arabs rebelling. He observed that the British were talking of)Tj-137 -12 TD 2.206 Tw (Arab transfer, and he asked whether they had a plan for implementation; whether )Tj394 0 TD 3.739 Tw (in fact)Tj-394 -12 TD 1.248 Tw (there could there be such a plan and whether it could be implemented. If not why were )Tj409 0 TD 0.709 Tc 0 Tw (the)Tj-409 -12 TD 0.349 Tc (British talking about it?! \()Tj/F4 7 Tf122 3 TD (2)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-100 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.446 Tw (Israel Idelson, a leading member )Tj154 0 TD 2.249 Tw (of the Kibbutz HaMe'uchad movement, spoke about)Tj-180 -12 TD 2.634 Tw (the demographic problem in Palestine and pointed out that no-one at that )Tj360 0 TD 1.592 Tw (meeting could)Tj-360 -12 TD 0.161 Tc 0 Tw (possibly believe that it would be possible within the near )Tj264 0 TD 0 Tc 1.883 Tw (future to implement what the Peel)Tj-264 -12 TD 0 Tw (Commission had proposed regarding Arab transfer. The Arabs would not transfer )Tj365 0 TD 4.707 Tw (voluntarily -)Tj-365 -12 TD 2.549 Tw (it was not in their )Tj93 0 TD 2.82 Tw (interests to move to Transjordan or Beersheba. Regarding compulsory)Tj-93 -12 TD 1.968 Tw (transfer, Idelson queried whether it )Tj169 0 TD 3.236 Tw (was implementable or desirable? Moshe Shertok then)Tj-169 -12 TD 0.683 Tw (interjected: "The compulsion comes )Tj162 0 TD 3.435 Tw (after the agreement." Idelson agreed with Shertok and)Tj-162 -12 TD 3.602 Tw (drew the parallel with the Greco-Turkish transfe