69 Tw (In this paper he dealt at length with transfer of Arabs under the heading )Tj376 0 TD 0.638 Tc 0 Tw ("The)Tj-402 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.201 Tw (Exchange of Land and Population". While stating that )Tj258 0 TD 3.37 Tw (this was by "far the most difficult)Tj-258 -12 TD 2.432 Tw (part of the whole scheme", he admitted that )Tj215 0 TD 2.544 Tw (there was "the encouraging precedent of the)Tj-215 -12 TD 0.045 Tc 0 Tw (compulsory shifting" of nearly two million Greeks and Turks. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf281 3 TD (4)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-259 -12 TD 0 Tc 3.629 Tw (After discussing details regarding demographic )Tj232 0 TD 7.975 Tw (distribution, availability of land,)Tj-258 -12 TD 0.511 Tw (surveying and funding, Coupland continued that )Tj224 0 TD 3.313 Tw ("the ideal would be the evacuation of all)Tj-224 -12 TD 2.403 Tw (Arabs and Jews from the Jew [sic] and Arab States respectively. This )Tj333 0 TD 6.295 Tw (ideal was actually)Tj-333 -12 TD 0.026 Tc 0 Tw (achieved in the Greco--Turkish exchange by a system of rigorous compulsion, the )Tj365 0 TD 0 Tc 4.614 Tw (hardships of)Tj-365 -12 TD 0.083 Tc 0 Tw (which have been compensated by the creation )Tj210 0 TD 0 Tc 2.086 Tw (of peace and amity." He pointed out that this)Tj-210 -12 TD 0.133 Tc 0 Tw (work had been made easier by virtue of the fact that both the Greek )Tj310 0 TD 0 Tc (and Turkish governments)Tj-310 -12 TD 0.029 Tc (had agreed and co-operated and because land )Tj207 0 TD 0 Tc 1.665 Tw (had been available "it could all be done in one)Tj-207 -12 TD -0.057 Tc 0 Tw (continuous vigorous 'push'." It )Tj136 0 TD 0 Tc 2.485 Tw (was, said Coupland, rather different in Palestine where there)Tj-136 -12 TD 0.15 Tc 0 Tw (was not a lot of land available and thus )Tj182 0 TD 0 Tc 1.788 Tw ("it is for consideration whether it might not be wise)Tj-182 -12 TD 0.144 Tc 0 Tw (to leave the exchange of )Tj112 0 TD 0 Tc 1.423 Tw (land and people during the Transition period on a voluntary basis.")Tj-112 -12 TD 0