D 1.253 Tw (Reginald Coupland, Professor of Colonial History at Oxford, whose knowledge and study )Tj416 0 TD 0 Tw (of)Tj-416 -12 TD 2.664 Tw (Colonial administration in the then British Colonial Empire )Tj286 0 TD 2.829 Tw (and in other colonial spheres)Tj-286 -12 TD 0 Tw (was well known to students throughout the world.)Tj26 -12 TD 1.546 Tw (This Commission \(popularly known as the "Peel Commission"\) arrived )Tj330 0 TD 3.389 Tw (in Palestine in)Tj-356 -12 TD -0.048 Tc 0 Tw (mid-November 1936 and during the course of the )Tj219 0 TD 0 Tc 0.351 Tw (next two months took evidence from over one)Tj-219 -12 TD 0.906 Tw (hundred witnesses. On their return )Tj163 0 TD 1.654 Tw (to England, the members of the Commission worked for)Tj-163 -12 TD 1.224 Tw (another six months on their Report and )Tj185 0 TD 2.566 Tw (at the end of June 1937 presented it to the British)Tj-185 -12 TD -0.092 Tc 0 Tw (Government. The Report was unanimous and consisted of over four hundred pages. It )Tj377 0 TD 0 Tc 1.384 Tw (included a)Tj-377 -12 TD 3.98 Tw (comprehensive and analytical survey of the )Tj219 0 TD 5.063 Tw (Palestine problem, an examination of the)Tj-219 -12 TD 0.173 Tc 0 Tw (operations of the Mandate, and proposals for "the possibility of a lasting settlement")Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 4.228 Tw (Chapter xxii of the Report dealt with a plan of partition. Under this plan, )Tj383 0 TD 0.709 Tc 0 Tw (the)Tj-409 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.412 Tw (Mandate would terminate and Palestine would be divided into )Tj294 0 TD 4.229 Tw (three areas: a Jewish State)Tj-294 -12 TD 0.066 Tc 0 Tw (including the whole of )Tj104 0 TD 0 Tc 2.777 Tw (the Galilee, the whole of the Jezreel Valley, the greater part of the)Tj-104 -12 TD 0.225 Tc 0 Tw (Beisan and all of the coastal plain from Ras el-Nakura )Tj252 0 TD 0 Tc 2.218 Tw (\(Rosh Hanikra\) in the north to Beer)Tj169 0 TD (-)Tj-421 -12 TD 0.141 Tc 0 Tw (Tuvia in the South; an Arab State containing the rest )Tj241 0 TD 0 Tc 1.766 Tw (of Palestine west of the Jordan together)Tj-241 -12 TD 6.168 Tw (with )Tj29 0 TD 5.561 Tw (Transjordan; a British enclave remaining under Mandate, containing Jerusalem,)Tj-29 -12 TD 2.976 Tw (Bethlehem and )Tj75 0 TD 2.251 Tw (Nazareth on a permanent basis and as a temporary measure the towns of)Tj-75 -12 TD 0.213 Tc 0 Tw (Haifa, Acre, Tiberias and Safed, which would ultimately become part of the Jewish State.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.612 Tw (There were nearly a quarter of a million Arabs within the boundaries of the )Tj358 0 TD -0.128 Tc 0 Tw (proposed)Tj-384 -12 TD 0.308 Tc (Jewish State )Tj60 0 TD 0 Tc 1.179 Tw (and about one and a half thousand Jews within the boundaries of the proposed)Tj-60 -12 TD 1.231 Tw (Arab State. This was seen by the members of the Peel Commission as a )Tj332 0 TD 0.987 Tw (serious problem and)Tj-332 -12 TD 0.099 Tc 0 Tw (section 10 of chapter xxii of the Report )Tj176 0 TD 0 Tc 2.047 Tw (dealt with this issue under the heading "Exchange of)Tj-176 -12 TD 0 Tw (Land and )Tj44 0 TD 1.957 Tw (Population." "If Partition is to be effective in promoting a final settlement it must)Tj/F5 7 Tf132 -40 TD 0.269 Tc 0 Tw (\321    191    \321)TjET
