e number of the Arabs you have in Palestine.'" We)Tj-129 -12 TD 0.086 Tc 0 Tw (should add that this transfer of Sudeten Germans )Tj225 0 TD 0 Tc 1.208 Tw (was a compulsory transfer approved by the)Tj-225 -12 TD 0 Tw (Great Powers.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.114 Tc (Ben-Horin answered Benes that he did "not have to sell me on the transfer )Tj338 0 TD 0 Tc 2.372 Tw (idea, because)Tj-364 -12 TD 4.302 Tw (I have advocated this solution for several years." )Tj251 0 TD 5.063 Tw (He then pointed out that whereas)Tj-251 -12 TD 0.151 Tc 0 Tw (President Hoover "also favors the )Tj156 0 TD 0 Tc 2.515 Tw (transfer idea", Weizmann and other Zionist leaders "may)Tj-156 -12 TD 1.574 Tw (not be far-sighted enough in this respect". He )Tj215 0 TD 2.868 Tw (also felt that one could not bring a parallel)Tj-215 -12 TD 5.168 Tw (with )Tj28 0 TD 3.923 Tw (the Sudeten Germans, since whereas Benes and his government were masters of)Tj-28 -12 TD 0.205 Tc 0 Tw (Czechoslovakia, this was not the case with the Jews of Palestine. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf303 3 TD (1)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj/F3 10 Tf-307 -36 TD -0.164 Tc (MOJLI AMIN, an Arab)Tj/F4 10 Tf26 -24 TD 0 Tc (In 1939, Mojli Amin, a member of the Arab Defense )Tj229 0 TD 1.71 Tw (Committee for Palestine put forward)Tj-255 -12 TD 0.117 Tc 0 Tw (a proposal for the transfer of Arabs from Palestine. This )Tj255 0 TD 0 Tc 1.198 Tw (proposal was published in Damascus)Tj-255 -12 TD 0.094 Tc 0 Tw (and distributed amongst the Arab leaders. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf197 3 TD (2)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-175 -12 TD 0 Tc (Amin began by blaming the suffering of the Arabs in )Tj236 0 TD 2.47 Tw (Palestine, the "lovers of peace", on)Tj-262 -12 TD 0 Tw (the Jews to whom )Tj81 0 TD 2.14 Tw (the British had promised "an Arab land on the basis of prehistoric fables)Tj-81 -12 TD 0.233 Tc 0 Tw (which state that Palestine is the designated land for Israel and )Tj291 0 TD 0 Tc 2.837 Tw (Judea." He added that there)Tj-291 -12 TD 1.075 Tw (was no democratic country who would protest to Britain on the evil )Tj315 0 TD 2.561 Tw (they were doing to the)Tj-315 -12 TD 0.167 Tc 0 Tw (Arabs.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.044 Tc (He then went on to put forward a solution which would satisfy the hopes of the Jews )Tj382 0 TD 0 Tc (and)Tj-408 -12 TD 0.111 Tc (put an end to the killing of the Arabs.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.203 Tc (Amin's proposal was that all of Palestine )Tj191 0 TD 0 Tc 1.53 Tw (be given to the Jews - its dwelling places, its)Tj-217 -12 TD 0.068 Tc 0 Tw (fields, its mosques, its )Tj101 0 TD 0 Tc 2.204 Tw (graveyards, etc. "Furthermore, I hereby propose that all the Arabs of)Tj-101 -12 TD 0.171 Tc 0 Tw (Palestine will leave and be divided up )Tj178 0 TD 0 Tc 0.594 Tw (amongst the neighbouring Arab countries. In exchange)Tj-178 -12 TD 1.862 Tw (for this, all the Jews living in Arab countries will leave and )Tj284 0 TD 2.892 Tw (come to Palestine." He added)Tj-284 -12 TD 0.064 Tc 0 Tw (that Palestine would be isolated from the Arab countries by means of "dams", so )Tj362 0 TD 0 Tc 3.043 Tw (that the Jews)Tj-362 -12 TD 0.112 Tc 0 Tw (would not see the Arabs and vice-versa. "We the )Tj222 0 TD 0 Tc 0.852 Tw (Arabs are prepared to accept upon ourselves)Tj-222 -12 TD 0.121 Tc 0 Tw (this great sacrifice for the sake of your welfare and the gathering in of your exiles and )Tj391 0 TD 0 Tc (because)Tj-391 -12 TD 0.058 Tc (of the generations of suffering which you underwent in Spain, Russia and other places.")Tj26 -12 TD 0.038 Tc (. Amin proposed that this exchange of population should be carried out )Tj322 0 TD 0 Tc 1.713 Tw (in the same way)Tj-348 -12 TD 0.089 Tc 0 Tw (as the Greco-Turkish population exchange, and that special committees should be )Tj371 0 TD 0.4 Tc (established)Tj-371 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.233 Tw (to deal with the liquidation of Jewish )Tj182 0 TD 3.575 Tw (and Arab property. He realised that at first there)Tj-182 -12 TD 0.124 Tc 0 Tw (would be great difficulties, but he hoped they would be finally solved.)TjET0