the Union of)Tj-114 -12 TD 0.079 Tc 0 Tw (Agricultural Labourers in Palestine. From 1932, he was Director of the Jewish )Tj350 0 TD 0 Tc 3.989 Tw (National Fund's)Tj-350 -12 TD 0.093 Tc 0 Tw (Land Development Division and played an important role in the acquisition )Tj346 0 TD 0 Tc 1.153 Tw (and development)Tj-346 -12 TD 0.127 Tc 0 Tw (of land for the Jewish National Fund and the planning of agricultural settlement.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.084 Tc (In his diary entry for 20 )Tj109 0 TD 0 Tc 1.244 Tw (December 1940, written in Jerusalem, Weitz wrote of a meeting)Tj-135 -12 TD 5.464 Tw (that he had had with the surveying engineer Zalman Lipschitz \(Lif\). )Tj363 0 TD 6.756 Tw (During their)Tj-363 -12 TD 0.119 Tc 0 Tw (conversation, Lipschitz spoke of the need to prepare material )Tj280 0 TD 0 Tc 1.033 Tw (in connection with the future of)Tj-280 -12 TD 2.039 Tw (Palestine. Such material would include )Tj185 0 TD 3.571 Tw (details of every Arab village, property ownership)Tj-185 -12 TD 0.142 Tc 0 Tw (and the possibility of developing intensive agriculture.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.092 Tc (Weitz answered, "It should be clear to us that there is no room in Palestine )Tj338 0 TD 0 Tc 1.65 Tw (for these two)Tj-364 -12 TD 1.117 Tw (peoples. No 'development' will bring us to our goal of independent nationhood in this )Tj399 0 TD 0.423 Tc 0 Tw (small)Tj-399 -12 TD 0.136 Tc (country. Without the )Tj98 0 TD 0 Tc 1.439 Tw (Arabs, the land will become wide and spacious for us; with the Arabs,)Tj-98 -12 TD 1.799 Tw (the land will remain sparse and cramped... The only solution is Palestine, at )Tj360 0 TD 5.449 Tw (least Western)Tj-360 -12 TD 0.06 Tc 0 Tw (Palestine, without Arabs. There is no room here for compromises!... The )Tj324 0 TD 0 Tc 2.004 Tw (way is to transfer the)Tj-324 -12 TD 3.362 Tw (Arabs from here to the neighbouring countries, all of them, except perhaps )Tj373 0 TD 4.363 Tw (those from)Tj-373 -12 TD 0.373 Tc 0 Tw (Bethlehem, Nazareth and the )Tj142 0 TD 0 Tc 2.074 Tw (Old City of Jerusalem." Although the vast majority of Arabs)Tj-142 -12 TD 0.127 Tc 0 Tw (in Palestine were Moslems, Weitz's )Tj162 0 TD 0 Tc 2.049 Tw (only exceptions referred to places which were especially)Tj-162 -12 TD 1.947 Tw (sacred to the Christian world and contained Christian )Tj256 0 TD 3.542 Tw (inhabitants. Possibly the reason for)Tj-256 -12 TD 3.011 Tw (these exceptions was to minimise opposition from )Tj245 0 TD 5.464 Tw (the Western Christian world to his)Tj-245 -12 TD 0.122 Tc 0 Tw (proposals.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.272 Tw (Weitz continued, "Not one )Tj125 0 TD 2.521 Tw (village, not one tribe should be left. And the form of the)Tj-151 -12 TD 0.055 Tc 0 Tw (transfer needs to be the creation of a refuge for them in Iraq, in Syria and )Tj328 0 TD 0 Tc 1.098 Tw (even in Transjordan.")Tj-328 -12 TD 0.261 Tc 0 Tw (He felt that for this objective, )Tj139 0 TD 0 Tc 0.621 Tw (large sums of money could be found. Only with such a transfer)Tj-139 -12 TD 0.051 Tc 0 Tw (would the land be able to absorb millions of Jews thus solving the Jewish problem. "There )Tj404 0 TD 0 Tc (is no)Tj-404 -12 TD 0.103 Tc (other way out," concluded Weitz.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 3.04 Tw (How did Lipschitz react to these proposals of Weitz's? The diary )Tj321 0 TD 4.352 Tw (entry notes that)Tj-347 -12 TD 0.138 Tc 0 Tw (Lipschitz agreed to these ideas regarding )Tj190 0 TD 0 Tc 1.67 Tw (the transfer of the Arabs from Palestine but added)Tj-190 -12 TD 2.991 Tw (that preparations should also be made for partial solutions. )Tj291 0 TD 5.352 Tw (To this Weitz replied that)Tj-291 -12 TD 3.301 Tw (investigations should )Tj104 0 TD 2.959 Tw (be made in the neighbouring countries in order to determine their)Tj-104 -12 TD 0.14 Tc 0 Tw (capacity to absorb the Arabs of Palestine. )Tj190 0 TD 0 Tc 2.123 Tw (Weitz notes that he and Lipschitz agreed between)Tj-190 -12 TD 1.799 Tw (them to apply to the )Tj101 0 TD 3.422 Tw (appropriate department and suggest that they 