ion was finance, which )Tj210 0 TD 1.662 Tw (would involve many millions of pounds.)Tj-236 -12 TD 0.34 Tw (These sums, Neumann considered, should be provided by )Tj263 0 TD 3.931 Tw (the Iraqi Government, the British)Tj-263 -12 TD 0.039 Tc 0 Tw (Government and the Jewish people.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.093 Tc (In conclusion, Neumann said, "What might have been regarded as fantastic )Tj342 0 TD 0 Tc 2.137 Tw (a generation)Tj-368 -12 TD 0.258 Tc 0 Tw (ago is the reality of to-day. Bold far-sighted statesmanship is wanted.")Tj26 -12 TD 0.147 Tc (At this period, Edward )Tj108 0 TD 0 Tc 0.922 Tw (Norman was quietly working on his own plan to transfer Arabs)Tj-134 -12 TD 0.081 Tc 0 Tw (from Palestine to )Tj79 0 TD 0 Tc 1.892 Tw (Iraq. From a letter written by RLE \(Rehabiah Lewin-Epstein ?\) to Norman)Tj-79 -12 TD 1.904 Tw (on 10 February \(the day of publication of Neumann's article in the "Palestine Review"\), )Tj412 0 TD 0 Tw (we)Tj-412 -12 TD 1.64 Tw (see that there was concern in American Zionist circles that )Tj276 0 TD 3.923 Tw (these newspaper articles might)Tj-276 -12 TD 0.101 Tc 0 Tw (harm Norman's negotiations.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.199 Tc (In this letter, RLE told )Tj105 0 TD 0 Tc 1.994 Tw (Norman that he had met Neumann the night before his article)Tj-131 -12 TD 0.265 Tc 0 Tw (had appeared in "Haboker". )Tj133 0 TD 0 Tc 1.955 Tw (When Neumann told RLE that his article would appear in the)Tj-133 -12 TD 4.9 Tw (newspapers the following day, RLE asked him to "recall it" since )Tj341 0 TD 4.532 Tw (someone, without)Tj-341 -12 TD -0.039 Tc 0 Tw (mentioning any names, was working on this behind the scenes, and )Tj299 0 TD 0 Tc 3.392 Tw ("the less publicity appears)Tj-299 -12 TD 2.008 Tw (on this subject, the better." In view of the fact that the article was not recalled, )Tj376 0 TD 1.803 Tw (RLE wrote)Tj-376 -12 TD 0.094 Tc 0 Tw (that apparently Neumann "was more interested in publicity than in my suggestion." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf385 3 TD (1)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-363 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.879 Tw (Five years later, )Tj81 0 TD 1.864 Tw (in February 1944, Neumann gave evidence before the Committee on)Tj-107 -12 TD 0.081 Tc 0 Tw (Foreign Affairs of the U.S. House of Representatives, on the question )Tj312 0 TD 0 Tc 3.676 Tw (of the "Jewish National)Tj-312 -12 TD 0.205 Tc 0 Tw (Home in Palestine".)Tj26 -12 TD 0.137 Tc (In the course of his evidence, he stated that "at no time in the long history of the )Tj366 0 TD 0.247 Tc (Zionist)Tj-392 -12 TD -0.067 Tc (movement in its )Tj73 0 TD 0 Tc -0.203 Tw (many conventions and congresses and public declarations and pronouncements)Tj-73 -12 TD 2.405 Tw (by its official spokesmen, at no )Tj153 0 TD 3.646 Tw (time in its long history has the Zionist movement ever)Tj-153 -12 TD 1.625 Tw (demanded the removal of the Arabs from Palestine. )Tj244 0 TD 3.512 Tw (The head of the Zionist Organization)Tj-244 -12 TD 0.233 Tc 0 Tw (has opposed it..." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf86 3 TD (2)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 0.069 Tc (\) Was Neumann "unaware" of what had been said on transfer )Tj278 0 TD 0 Tc 2.658 Tw (by the head)Tj-368 -12 TD 2.955 Tw (of the Zionist Organization and its official spokesmen at \(for example\) )Tj345 0 TD 5.388 Tw (the 20th Zionist)Tj-345 -12 TD 0 Tw (Congress?!)Tj26 -12 TD 1.767 Tw (Two years )Tj52 0 TD 3.068 Tw (later, on 8 January 1948, Neumann again gave evidence before a public)Tj-78 -12 TD 1.48 Tw (committee. This time it was the Anglo-American Committee of Inquiry )Tj331 0 TD 2.64 Tw (on Palestine and he)Tj-331 -12 TD 0 Tw (represented the American Zionist Emergency Council.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.151 Tc (During cross-examination, the British Conservative )Tj237 0 TD 0 Tc 1.326 Tw (M.P. Major Reginald Manningham)Tj158 0 TD (-)Tj-421 -12 TD 1.606 Tw (Buller asked Neumann: "I )Tj123 0 TD 2.746 Tw (wasn't quite clear, when you were dealing with the population)Tj-123 -12 TD 0.104 Tc 0 Tw (outside Palestine, whether you were )Tj167 0 TD 0 Tc 0.652 Tw (or were not suggesting that in the course of time some of)Tj-167 -12 TD 0.094 Tc 0 Tw (the Arab population within Palestine might move or be moved outside.")Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.082 Tw (To this Neumann answered: "No, sir. I made no such suggestion.... We have never, )Tj383 0 TD 0.709 Tc 0 Tw (the)Tj-409 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.219 Tw (Zionist movement has never, suggested the displacement of a single Arab )Tj353 0 TD 5.672 Tw (from Palestine.)Tj-353 -12 TD 0.792 Tw (There is no need for it. And we )Tj146 0 TD 1.668 Tw (would under no circumstances base the creation of a Jewish)Tj-146 -12 TD 0 Tw (policy upon the )Tj72 0 TD 1.565 Tw (forced removal of people who have lived there for centuries.... I would only)Tj-72 -12 TD 0.164 Tc 0 Tw (like to say to you, sir, that the suggestion regarding that idea was made by the British )Tj394 0 TD -0.18 Tc (Labour)TjET0.24 w 85.12 131.88 m 228.12 131.88 l S 1 w BT/F4 7 Tf85.5 119 TD (1)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0 Tc ( / RLE to Norman, 10 February 1939, \(CZA A251/17a\).)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (2)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 3.047 Tw ( / "The Jewish National Home in Palestine", Hearings before the Committee on Foreign Affairs )Tj383 0 TD 3.898 Tw (House of)Tj-387 -9 TD 0 Tw (Representatives, February 8, 9, 15 and 16, 1944, Washington D.C., 1944, p.307.)Tj/F5 7 Tf176 -31 TD 0.269 Tc (\321    136    \321)TjET
