nial Office and)Tj-314 -12 TD 0.118 Tc 0 Tw (Foreign Office utilised this fact to deny Bell an exit permit and hence prevented any chance )Tj416 0 TD 0 Tc (of)Tj-416 -12 TD 1.059 Tw (implementing Norman's plan. We now know that during the Second World )Tj349 0 TD 4.421 Tw (War, officers at)Tj-349 -12 TD 0.212 Tc 0 Tw (the British Passport Control Office )Tj162 0 TD 0 Tc 0.705 Tw ("were not regular foreign service employees, but members)Tj-162 -12 TD 0.119 Tc 0 Tw (of MI6 [the British Secret Service] seconded to the Foreign office as a cover." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf350 3 TD (6)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-328 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.541 Tw (In a book by Eliahu Ben-Horin which was published in 1943, the author )Tj339 0 TD 2.993 Tw (observed, "A)Tj-365 -12 TD 0.116 Tc 0 Tw (certain project dealing with the transfer of the Palestinian Arabs to Iraq was welcomed by )Tj409 0 TD 0.709 Tc (the)Tj-409 -12 TD 0.047 Tc (Iraqian Government. The outbreak of the )Tj186 0 TD 0 Tc 1.778 Tw (war unfortunately interrupted the negotiations over)Tj-186 -12 TD 0.214 Tc 0 Tw (the materialisation of such a project." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf178 3 TD (7)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-156 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.085 Tw (Ben-Horin did not mention the author of the project by name, but it )Tj315 0 TD 3.76 Tw (seems very likely)Tj-341 -12 TD 4.625 Tw (that he is referring to Norman's plan, since )Tj228 0 TD 6.519 Tw (unlike the instigators of several other)Tj-228 -12 TD 0 Tw (contemporary proposals for the transfer of Arabs to Iraq, Norman did not just make )Tj373 0 TD 2.962 Tw (a proposal,)Tj-373 -12 TD 0.125 Tc 0 Tw (but entered into actual negotiations via Bell on its implementation.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.366 Tc (The historian Rafael )Tj99 0 TD 0 Tc 1.783 Tw (Medoff is also of the view that the transfer proposal brought by)Tj-125 -12 TD 0.064 Tc 0 Tw (Ben-Horin in his book is the proposal by )Tj184 0 TD 0 Tc 1.899 Tw (Norman. Furthermore Medoff holds that "it may be)Tj-184 -12 TD 1.087 Tw (that Norman was the sou