he Peel Commission report in 1937,)Tj-40 -12 TD 0 Tw (Thon )Tj25 0 TD 1.281 Tw (was an enthusiastic supporter of Arab transfer from Palestine and an active member of)Tj-25 -12 TD 0.071 Tc 0 Tw (the Jewish Agency Population Transfer Committee.)Tj26 -12 TD -0.039 Tc (In August 1942 the members of a Jewish-Arab )Tj204 0 TD 0 Tc 1.778 Tw (relations committee, of which Thon was a)Tj-230 -12 TD 1.64 Tw (member, wrote a report )Tj114 0 TD 3.221 Tw (on future Jewish-Arab relations. Thon's views on, amongst other)Tj-114 -12 TD 1.866 Tw (things, the transfer of Arabs from Palestine, )Tj208 0 TD 2.116 Tw (could not find expression in this report of the)Tj-208 -12 TD 0 Tw (committee, and so he submitted a personal memorandum in November of that year.)Tj26 -12 TD 1.218 Tw (After discussing the continual )Tj140 0 TD 2.328 Tw (danger the Arabs would pose to a future Jewish State,)Tj-166 -12 TD 0.194 Tc 0 Tw (even if they were in the minority, Thon wrote that "a Jewish State )Tj304 0 TD 0 Tc 2.005 Tw (would only have value, if)Tj-304 -12 TD 2.144 Tw (together with its proclamation by )Tj161 0 TD 2.675 Tw (the Deciding Powers, a transfer of the Arab population)Tj-161 -12 TD 1.489 Tw (would also be made possible." He however added that such a transfer would have )Tj387 0 TD 1.432 Tw (to be by)Tj-387 -12 TD 1.44 Tw (agreement with the Arabs. He went on to explain: "One )Tj262 0 TD 2.468 Tw (should not suppose that the Peace)Tj-262 -12 TD 0.637 Tw (Conference, whose function it would be to make peace )Tj250 0 TD 1.897 Tw (between peoples and to recognise the)Tj-250 -12 TD 2.028 Tw (natural rights of all peoples, will agree to the removal of the Arabs of Palestine )Tj380 0 TD 3.228 Tw (by force.")Tj-380 -12 TD 2.01 Tw (Thon did not believe that after the War, there would be place for the Nazis' )Tj364 0 TD 2.46 Tw (views on the)Tj-364 -12 TD -0.054 Tc 0 Tw (transference of minorities from country to country. He )Tj240 0 TD 0 Tc 1.584 Tw (could thus not visualise that in the new)Tj-240 -12 TD -0.082 Tc 0 Tw (Europe, tens of millions of people could be uprooted )Tj231 0 TD 0 Tc 1.531 Tw (from their homes and lands. [In fact, time)Tj-231 -12 TD -0.025 Tc 0 Tw (showed Thon to be wrong! Following the second world war, the )Tj285 0 TD 0 Tc 2.148 Tw (Allies did in fact agree to the)Tj-285 -12 TD 2.977 Tw (transfer of almost ten million persons in Europe.] Thon was also of the opinion )Tj392 0 TD 8.156 Tw (that a)Tj-392 -12 TD 0.022 Tc 0 Tw (compulsory transfer of Arabs would result in a strong reaction by influential Diaspora Jews.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 0.677 Tw (He then went on )Tj79 0 TD 2.36 Tw (to discuss transfer from the point of view of the Arabs. On this he)Tj-105 -12 TD 2.653 Tw (wrote, "One should not however exclude the fact that also )Tj285 0 TD 4.182 Tw (the Arabs will recognise the)Tj-285 -12 TD 0.146 Tc 0 Tw (advantages which will accrue to them in their transfer from )Tj274 0 TD 0 Tc 2.319 Tw (Palestine to the Arab countries.")Tj-274 -12 TD 1.766 Tw (He brought a proof )Tj95 0 TD 2.887 Tw (from the transfer of Greeks and how it caused Greece to grow both)Tj-95 -12 TD 2.433 Tw (economically and militarily. Similarly, the Arab countries were lacking in )Tj351 0 TD 3.199 Tw (population, and)Tj-351 -12 TD 0.081 Tc 0 Tw (this would be rectified by an influx of Arabs from Palestine.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.084 Tc (Thon concluded that the Zionist )Tj147 0 TD 0 Tc 1.837 Tw (aspirations should thus be for "an agreement with the)Tj-173 -12 TD 0.069 Tc 0 Tw (Palestinian Arabs and the neighbouring countries for a transfer of population." )Tj356 0 TD 0 Tc 0.889 Tw (He pointed out)Tj-356 -12 TD 0.155 Tc 0 Tw (that to achieve this, one needs to make every effort and utilise every )Tj314 0 TD 0 Tc 1.999 Tw (outside influence. "Only)Tj-314 -12 TD 0 Tw (if such an )Tj45 0 TD 2.128 Tw (agreement is achieved, will a Jewish State be able to arise in our days." Without)Tj-45 -12 TD 1.006 Tw (such an agreement, Thon felt that it would be necessary to continue )Tj313 0 TD 3.67 Tw (with the Mandate over)Tj-313 -12 TD 0.045 Tc 0 Tw (Palestine and maintain a force which would be strong enough to maintain security. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf377 3 TD (2)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj/F3 10 Tf-381 -36 TD 0 Tc (EDWARD NORMAN)Tj0 -24 TD -0.231 Tc (Introduction)Tj/F4 10 Tf26 -12 TD -0.029 Tc (Edward Norman, who was an American )Tj181 0 TD 0 Tc 5.46 Tw (multimillionaire, financier and philanthropist)Tj-207 -12 TD 0.039 Tc 0 Tw (was born in 1900. His grandfather, Emanuel Nusbaum, was a poor Bavarian Jewish )Tj374 0 TD 0.143 Tc (immigrant,)TjET0.24 w 85.12 122.88 m 228.12 122.88 l S 1 w BT/F4 7 Tf85.5 110 TD (1)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.05 Tc ( / Thon to Kisch, 2 June 1931, \(CZA S25/9836\).)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (2)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0 Tc ( / Personal memorandum by Dr. J. Thon, 3 November 1942, p.2, \(CZA S25/204\).)Tj/F5 7 Tf174 -31 TD 0.25 Tc (\321    84    \321)TjET
