ary Council of the Jews)Tj-265 -12 TD 0.197 Tc 0 Tw (of Palestine which was established in 1918. At its fifth session, held in )Tj324 0 TD 0 Tc 1.484 Tw (Jaffa in June 1919, the)Tj-324 -12 TD 0.025 Tc 0 Tw (question of transfer of Arabs from Palestine was raised by )Tj260 0 TD 0 Tc 2.437 Tw (Yosef Sprinzak, a leader of Hapoel)Tj-260 -12 TD 0.308 Tc 0 Tw (Hazair, who )Tj61 0 TD 0 Tc 1.805 Tw (said that "we must receive Palestine without any reduction or restrictions. But)Tj-61 -12 TD 0.554 Tw (there is a known quantum of Arabs )Tj163 0 TD 3.358 Tw (who live in Palestine and they will receive their due.)Tj-163 -12 TD 0.039 Tc 0 Tw (Anyone who wants to work will cultivate his plot. Anyone who does )Tj310 0 TD 0 Tc 1.553 Tw (not want to work it, will)Tj-310 -12 TD 0.065 Tc 0 Tw (receive compensation and he will seek his fortune in another country." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf322 3 TD (5)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-300 -12 TD 0.086 Tc (The words "he will seek his fortune in another country" have been heavily crossed out )Tj390 0 TD 0 Tc (in)Tj-416 -12 TD 1.068 Tw (these minutes. As )Tj84 0 TD 2.275 Tw (we can see in various other places in this book, proposals made for the)Tj-84 -12 TD 1.732 Tw (transfer of Arabs from Palestine, have often )Tj207 0 TD 1.204 Tw (been crossed out or even deleted from minutes,)Tj-207 -12 TD 3.827 Tw (letters, etc. In this particular case, the historian Tom Segev comments: )Tj352 0 TD 7.513 Tw ("That the full)Tj-352 -12 TD 0.094 Tc 0 Tw (implications of this statement were understood by all is )Tj253 0 TD 0 Tc 1.552 Tw (indicated by the fact it is crossed out)Tj-253 -12 TD 0.096 Tc 0 Tw (in the meeting's minutes." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf123 3 TD (6)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-101 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.542 Tw (Just over a decade later, in the early 1930s, a problem which surfaced was what to )Tj388 0 TD 0 Tw (do)Tj-414 -12 TD 1.262 Tw (with Arab tenants who occupied land )Tj177 0 TD 2.667 Tw (which had been acquired by the Zionists for Jewish)T