of this Zionism is )Tj255 0 TD 0 Tc 1.156 Tw (the transfer of a people from country)Tj-255 -12 TD -0.035 Tc 0 Tw (to country - a transfer by agreement. For an agreed immigration I do not agree, but for an )Tj394 0 TD 0 Tc (agreed)Tj-394 -12 TD (transfer I am prepared to agree in regard to our neighbours.")Tj26 -12 TD 1.848 Tw (He pointed out that the Zionists held that transfer was one of the great )Tj340 0 TD 6.124 Tw (ideas which)Tj-366 -12 TD 0.119 Tc 0 Tw (was taking )Tj52 0 TD 0 Tc 0.971 Tw (place in the world - in some places in a very good manner but in others in a very)Tj-52 -12 TD 2.737 Tw (bad one. He said that the Zionists had never abandoned the idea of transfer )Tj374 0 TD 3.955 Tw (when it is)Tj-374 -12 TD 1.859 Tw (carried out in a fair manner, and felt that the developments which might )Tj347 0 TD 1.935 Tw (come about after)Tj-347 -12 TD 0.104 Tc 0 Tw (the termination of the Second World War could very possibly lead to an agreed transfer.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.513 Tw (Katznelson then continued: "Since I have entered into this argument, )Tj321 0 TD 3.417 Tw (we will see this)Tj-347 -12 TD 4.293 Tw (question through: Was the establishment of Merchavia accomplished without )Tj384 0 TD 0.247 Tc 0 Tw (transfer?)Tj-384 -12 TD 0 Tc (There was indeed transfer of one )Tj148 0 TD 1.77 Tw (or two Arab villages, by agreement with the Jews; was this)Tj-148 -12 TD 1.623 Tw (unfair or unethical? This we arranged in a small )Tj229 0 TD 3.104 Tw (area of Palestine for the sake of a small)Tj-229 -12 TD 1.672 Tw (settlement. And the members of Hashomer Hazair are dwelling )Tj299 0 TD 3.772 Tw (in Merchavia, in Mishmar)Tj-299 -12 TD 0.076 Tc 0 Tw (Haemek - is this not transfer, moving )Tj170 0 TD 0 Tc 1.578 Tw (of [Arab] population from place to .place? If transfer is)Tj-170 -12 TD 0.105 Tc 0 Tw (unethical from the outset, then the settlement on )Tj222 0 TD 0 Tc 2.663 Tw (the land by Hashomer Hazair is unethical,)Tj-222 -12 TD 0.066 Tc 0 Tw (because it utilises the moving of population from place to place, )Tj289 0 TD 0 Tc 1.067 Tw (and it is not only we who are)Tj-289 -12 TD 0 Tw (making use of transfer." He concluded by pointing out that )Tj263 0 TD 1.251 Tw (the Jews were enjoying the benefits)Tj-263 -12 TD 2.31 Tw (from the small transfer that had taken place )Tj214 0 TD 2.841 Tw (in Palestine during the previous sixty years.)Tj-214 -12 TD 0.159 Tc 0 Tw ("Therefore Ya'ari should not reject this idea, reject it on ethical grounds." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf338 3 TD (3)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-316 -12 TD 0.118 Tc (A detailed study of )Tj90 0 TD 0 Tc 1.961 Tw (the character of Berl Katznelson has been made by his biographer)Tj-116 -12 TD 0.515 Tc 0 Tw (Anita Shapira. With )Tj101 0 TD 0 Tc 1.986 Tw (regards to his attitude towards transfer, she wrote that Berl saw in a)Tj-101 -12 TD 0.093 Tc 0 Tw (mutually agreed transfer a real answer to )Tj189 0 TD 0 Tc 2.074 Tw (the Arab problem in Palestine. From the time that)Tj-189 -12 TD 0.074 Tc 0 Tw (the Peel Commission put forward this proposal, he was very enchanted )Tj324 0 TD 0 Tc 2.347 Tw (with the idea. Just as)Tj-324 -12 TD 2.159 Tw (transfer )Tj39 0 TD 2.623 Tw (had solved the Greco-Turkish conflict, Berl saw it as a long term solution to the)Tj-39 -12 TD 3.127 Tw (Jewish-Arab conflict. He was therefore very pleased when the )Tj304 0 TD 4.378 Tw (British Labour party put)Tj-304 -12 TD 0.188 Tc 0 Tw (forward transfer of Arabs as part of its Palestine policy. Shapira )Tj296 0 TD 0 Tc 2.337 Tw (concluded that Katznelson's)Tj-296 -12 TD 4.968 Tw ("thoughts on population transfer were characteristic of )Tj279 0 TD 5.428 Tw (him; he did not recoil from)Tj-279 -12 TD 0.02 Tc 0 Tw (revolutionary changes, from audacious exchanges, and he )Tj260 0 TD 0 Tc 3.58 Tw (believed that the aftermath of the)Tj-260 -12 TD -0.097 Tc 0 Tw ([second world] war would be the opportune moment for change." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf291 3 TD (4)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj/F3 1