ber dealing )Tj264 0 TD 2.96 Tw (with population transfer. Some of)Tj-264 -12 TD 1.66 Tw (these articles were concerned with general )Tj200 0 TD 3.709 Tw (ideas on transfer, whilst others dealt with his)Tj-200 -12 TD 0.11 Tc 0 Tw (specific proposals for the transfer of Arabs from Palestine.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.134 Tc (Sharon first put forward his views )Tj159 0 TD 0 Tc 1.376 Tw (on population transfer in 1916. In a series of articles)Tj-185 -12 TD 0.115 Tc 0 Tw (entitled "A Revision of Pacifism", published in the July-October 1916 issue of )Tj350 0 TD 0 Tc 3.55 Tw (the pacifist and)Tj-350 -12 TD 4.837 Tw (anti-imperialist journal "Dokuments )Tj177 0 TD 6.026 Tw (des Forschritts", Sharon attempted to apply "the)Tj-177 -12 TD 0.244 Tc 0 Tw (framework of the Zionist idea to other nationalities, that )Tj265 0 TD 0 Tc 1.99 Tw (is to solve their national problems)Tj-265 -12 TD 0.018 Tc 0 Tw (by an agreed and organised transfer of a nation or parts of it to )Tj281 0 TD 0 Tc 3.345 Tw (the territory of another state.")Tj-281 -12 TD (\()Tj/F4 7 Tf4 3 TD (2)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj18 -12 TD 0 Tw (Dr. Moshe Yegar, who made an intensive study of )Tj225 0 TD 0.889 Tw (the writings of Sharon, commented on)Tj-251 -12 TD 0.117 Tc 0 Tw (the above passage, "In other words, the transfer of )Tj230 0 TD 0 Tc 2.134 Tw (the Palestinian Arabs to the neighbouring)Tj-230 -12 TD 0.099 Tc 0 Tw (countries and the transfer of Diaspora Jewry to Palestine, as the only )Tj312 0 TD 0 Tc 2.33 Tw (solution of the Palestine)Tj-312 -12 TD 1.422 Tw (problem." According )Tj98 0 TD 3.93 Tw (to Yegar, Sharon would sometimes claim that he was the original)Tj-98 -12 TD 3.457 Tw (proposer of this idea. As )Tj128 0 TD 4.294 Tw (Yegar commented, Sharon was obviously unaware of earlier)Tj-128 -12 TD 0.249 Tc 0 Tw (proposals, "Nevertheless, )Tj121 0 TD 0 Tc 1.993 Tw (there was nobody within the Zionist movement like Sharon with)Tj-121 -12 TD 2.132 Tw (his constant preaching and insistance