tly steal )Tj68 0 TD 0 Tc 2.115 Tw (away". He felt sure that the Jews would be prepared to pay their travelling)Tj-68 -12 TD 0 Tw (expenses and purchase any immovable property.)Tj26 -12 TD 1.404 Tw (In conclusion, Zangwill wrote that )Tj162 0 TD 3.071 Tw (the Jews of Palestine, if a minority, would either)Tj-188 -12 TD 1.49 Tw (have to dominate the majority or be )Tj171 0 TD 3.268 Tw (dominated by them and neither of these alternatives)Tj-171 -12 TD 3.762 Tw (would be desirable. "Neither would be the dream that has sweetened the centuries )Tj416 0 TD 0 Tw (of)TjET0.24 w 85.12 130.88 m 228.12 130.88 l S 1 w BT/F4 7 Tf85.5 118 TD (1)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD ( / Vladimir Jabotinsky, "A Conversation with Zangwill", Der Moment, \(Warsaw\), no.152, )Tj316 0 TD 1.199 Tw (21 July 1939, \(news-clipping)Tj-320 -9 TD 1.937 Tw (in Jabotinsky Archives 1939/18 tav no.17\); Writings of Jabotinsky vol.17, \(Zichronot ben-dori\), \(Tel-Aviv, )Tj398 0 TD 0.183 Tc 0 Tw ([n.d.]\),)Tj-398 -9 TD 0 Tc (pp.256-59; Jewish Herald, \(Johannesburg\), vol.iii, no.21, 4 August 1939, p.5.)Tj/F5 7 Tf178 -31 TD 0.25 Tc (\321    56    \321)TjET
