hich they would learn )Tj373 0 TD 2.962 Tw (Arabic and)Tj-373 -12 TD 0.1 Tc 0 Tw (Hebrew, thus increasing the Arabs' cultural level and developing )Tj297 0 TD 0 Tc -0.444 Tw (a common language between)Tj-297 -12 TD 0.131 Tc 0 Tw (the two peoples. Zangwill was not happy with Ben-Yehuda's answer and )Tj335 0 TD 0 Tc 3.636 Tw (felt that his vision)Tj-335 -12 TD 2.127 Tw (of the Hebrew language had distorted his objectivity. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf258 3 TD (3)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 1.49 Tw (\) However, it took )Tj89 0 TD 3.709 Tw (Zangwill a few)Tj-351 -12 TD 0.039 Tc 0 Tw (years to formulate his own solution to the Arab problem.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.392 Tw (In the December 1904 edition of the American Jewish newspaper "The )Tj338 0 TD 0.256 Tc 0 Tw (Maccabaean")Tj-364 -12 TD 0.175 Tc (appeared an article by Zangwill entitled "Zionism and England's Offer". )Tj333 0 TD 0 Tc 1.253 Tw (In the course of this)Tj-333 -12 TD 0.165 Tc 0 Tw (article Zangwill put forward his proposal for the transfer )Tj264 0 TD 0 Tc 2.109 Tw (of Arabs from Palestine: "There is,)Tj-264 -12 TD 0.17 Tc 0 Tw (however, a difficulty from which the Zionist dares not avert his eyes, though )Tj355 0 TD 0 Tc 3.909 Tw (he rarely likes)Tj-355 -12 TD 1.973 Tw (to face it. Palestine proper has already its inhabitants.... So we must be prepared )Tj383 0 TD 5.257 Tw (either to)Tj-383 -12 TD 0 Tw (drive out by the )Tj74 0 TD 1.456 Tw (sword the tribes in possession as our forefathers did, or to grapple with the)Tj-74 -12 TD 0 Tw (problem of )Tj52 0 TD 2.14 Tw (a large alien population, mostly Mohammedan and accustomed for centuries to)Tj-52 -12 TD 0 Tw (despise us." He )Tj71 0 TD 2.399 Tw (also felt that the Zionists must extend their "idea of Palestine", mentioning)Tj-71 -12 TD 0.079 Tc 0 Tw (the Euphrates, the border of Egypt and Mesopotamia \(Iraq\) as her true boundaries. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf379 3 TD (4)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-357 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.519 Tw (In a half-page )Tj71 0 TD 3.141 Tw (advert