 TD 0.04 Tc 0 Tw (just division of the subjugated empire.")Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.638 Tw (Syrkin hoped that )Tj90 0 TD 2.285 Tw (the European states would be in favour of Jews settling Palestine)Tj-116 -12 TD 1.347 Tw (since the Europeans would thus free themselves of their )Tj262 0 TD 3.791 Tw (Jewish population whilst enabling)Tj-262 -12 TD 1.917 Tw (Asia to develop both economically and culturally. However, Syrkin )Tj318 0 TD 3.956 Tw (urged that if after all)Tj-318 -12 TD 0.059 Tc 0 Tw (their efforts the Jews were unsuccessful in obtaining Palestine, they should chose )Tj365 0 TD 0 Tc 3.56 Tw (another land)TjET0.24 w 85.12 152.88 m 228.12 152.88 l S 1 w BT/F4 7 Tf85.5 140 TD (1)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.025 Tc 0 Tw ( / Boris Guriel, Letters to the Editor, Jewish Observer and Middle East Review, \(London\), 6 Marc1964, p.21.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (2)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.04 Tc ( / Leon Simon, Letters to the Editor, Jewish Observer and Middle East Review, \(London\), 13 March 1964, p.25.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (3)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.021 Tc ( / Ilan Amitzur, America, Britain and Palestine, \(Jerusalem, 1979\), p.128.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (4)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.02 Tc ( / Nedava, Forum \(on the Jewish People, Zionism and Israel\), op. cit., p.104.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (5)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD -0.032 Tc ( / Christopher Sykes, Cross Roads to Israel, \(London, 1965\), p.312.)Tj/F5 7 Tf174 -31 TD 0.25 Tc (\321    49    \321)TjET
