48 -12 TD 0.117 Tc 0 Tw (However, it shows that the minutes were written )Tj225 0 TD 0 Tc 0.682 Tw (up by someone on the Zionist side, if not by)Tj-225 -12 TD 0.159 Tc 0 Tw (Weizmann himself. There was )Tj141 0 TD 0 Tc 1.359 Tw (obviously something in these minutes that Weizmann did not)Tj-141 -12 TD 0.222 Tc 0 Tw (want Rothschild to see!)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 4.706 Tw (At the end of the meeting, Weizmann was charged with the preparation of )Tj393 0 TD (a)Tj-419 -12 TD -0.099 Tc 0 Tw (memorandum which he began by )Tj149 0 TD 0 Tc 2.154 Tw (stating that there was "general agreement on the following)Tj-149 -12 TD 5.259 Tw (points." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf45 3 TD (3)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 3.827 Tw (\) in connection with transfer, Weizmann wrote, "In that State )Tj309 0 TD 5.998 Tw (there will be)Tj-358 -12 TD 0.18 Tc 0 Tw (complete civil )Tj67 0 TD 0 Tc 2.22 Tw (and political equality of rights for all citizens, without distinction of race or)Tj-67 -12 TD 0.132 Tc 0 Tw (religion, and in addition the Arabs will enjoy full )Tj226 0 TD 0 Tc 1.659 Tw (autonomy in their own internal affairs, but)Tj-226 -12 TD 0.2 Tc 0 Tw (if any Arabs did not wish to remain in a Jewish State, every facility will )Tj332 0 TD 0 Tc 0.947 Tw (be given to them for)Tj-332 -12 TD 0.04 Tc 0 Tw (transfer to one of the many and vast Arab countries." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf242 3 TD (4)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 0 Tc (\) )Tj6 0 TD 2.24 Tw (Here, the transfer of Arabs is clearly)Tj-252 -12 TD 0.089 Tc 0 Tw (of a voluntary nature. However, this does not necessarily reflect Weizmann's personal view )Tj415 0 TD 0 Tc (as)Tj-415 -12 TD 5.075 Tw (the memorandum summarised the "general agreement" of the meeting. Most of )Tj409 0 TD 0.709 Tc 0 Tw (the)Tj-409 -12 TD 0 Tc 4.143 Tw (participants were hostile )Tj124 0 TD 3.96 Tw (to Zionism and the establishment of a Jewish State and had)Tj-124 -12 TD 2.905 Tw (expressed great concern at this meeting on the future )Tj263 0 TD 5.279 Tw (of the non-Jewish inhabitants of)Tj-263 -12 TD 4.199 Tw (Palestine. Unlike the )Tj106 0 TD 3.006 Tw (minutes, this memorandum was sent to Anthony de Rothschild to)Tj-106 -12 TD 0.179 Tc 0 Tw (distribute to the friends he had invited to this meeting. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf258 3 TD (5)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-236 -12 TD 0.036 Tc (A few months later, Weizmann publicly endorsed )Tj225 0 TD 0 Tc 2.294 Tw (transfer, albeit of a voluntary nature,)Tj-251 -12 TD 1.55 Tw (when he repeated almost word for word in the American journal "Foreign Affairs" what )Tj413 0 TD 0.695 Tc 0 Tw (he)Tj-413 -12 TD 0.026 Tc (had written on transfer in this memorandum. \()Tj/F4 7 Tf208 3 TD (6)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj/F3 10 Tf-212 -24 TD -0.048 Tc (Attitude of Weizmann towards Transfer)Tj/F4 10 Tf26 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.486 Tw (Following tributes paid to Weizmann on the B.B.C.'s Third Programme in )Tj355 0 TD 0 Tw (December)Tj-381 -12 TD -0.156 Tc (1963, the correspondence columns )Tj149 0 TD 0 Tc 1.954 Tw (of the "Jewish Observer and Middle East Review" included)Tj-149 -12 TD 0.083 Tc 0 Tw (an argument as to Weizmann's attitude towards the transfer of Arabs. Boris Guriel, Director )Tj416 0 TD 0 Tc (of)Tj-416 -12 TD 2.137 Tw (the Weizmann Archives, claimed that Weizmann had favoured transfer; Sir Leon )Tj384 0 TD 2.733 Tw (Simon, a)Tj-384 -12 TD 0.229 Tc 0 Tw (leading British Zionist, took the opposite view.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.103 Tc (To substantiate his case, Guriel )Tj143 0 TD 0 Tc 1.834 Tw (quoted a letter that Weizmann had written to Sir Leon)Tj-169 -12 TD 0.615 Tw (Simon in November 1941. "I can see no reason why we could not do the )Tj328 0 TD 4.018 Tw (same thing that the)Tj-328 -12 TD 0.222 Tc 0 Tw (Greeks did after the last war. Whether it would take five years or three )Tj331 0 TD 0 Tc 2.119 Tw (or seven, whether it)Tj-331 -12 TD -0.079 Tc 0 Tw (would be two million or )Tj108 0 TD 0 Tc 2.189 Tw (three, I cannot say." Guriel claimed that Weizmann was advocating)Tj-108 -12 TD 0.141 Tc 0 Tw (applying