tion plan, including sovereignty; the inclusion of the )Tj326 0 TD 0 Tc -0.407 Tw (new Jewish suburbs of)Tj-326 -12 TD 0.251 Tc 0 Tw (Jerusalem within the Jewish State; the potash )Tj213 0 TD 0 Tc 1.672 Tw (and the Rutenberg electric works; the transfer)Tj-213 -12 TD 2.719 Tw (of population and the transition period. After this meeting, Weizmann wrote )Tj372 0 TD 0 Tw (a document)Tj-372 -12 TD (recording the substance of the meeting.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.118 Tc (A few weeks later )Tj84 0 TD 0 Tc 2.2 Tw (in Zurich, Meir Grossman, leader of the Jewish State Party, \(which)Tj-110 -12 TD 2.632 Tw (was a splinter group of the Revisionists\), )Tj201 0 TD 3.913 Tw (informed the twentieth Zionist Congress, then)Tj-201 -12 TD 0 Tw (debating )Tj42 0 TD 2.516 Tw (the Peel Report, that he had evidence that Weizmann had already agreed to the)Tj-42 -12 TD 3.99 Tw (partition proposals. "I have in my hand )Tj204 0 TD 4.658 Tw (a document which contains the details of a)Tj-204 -12 TD 1.089 Tw (conversation held between Weizmann and Ormsby-Gore. In this conversation )Tj357 0 TD 2.966 Tw (they discussed)Tj-357 -12 TD 0.068 Tc 0 Tw (the conditions under which - if accepted - )Tj189 0 TD 0 Tc 1.916 Tw (Weizmann would support the partition proposals.")Tj-189 -12 TD 0.04 Tc 0 Tw (Grossman went on to accuse Weizmann of two-faced politics, claiming that without )Tj376 0 TD 0 Tc (permission)Tj-376 -12 TD 0.024 Tc (of the Congress or the Zionist General Council, Weizmann had gone to the )Tj334 0 TD 0 Tc 3.3 Tw (British Government)Tj-334 -12 TD 1.5 Tw (and prejudiced the Congress's deliberations. "I )Tj217 0 TD 2.516 Tw (find Weizmann guilty of a severe breach of)Tj-217 -12 TD 0.351 Tc 0 Tw (discipline." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf60 3 TD (4)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-38 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.704 Tw (The purloined document was reproduced in full a few days )Tj293 0 TD 5.872 Tw (later by "The Jewish)Tj-319 -12 TD 0 Tw (Chronicle". The document began )Tj147 0 TD 1.311 Tw (by describing how Or