 Tc 1.908 Tw (free of Arabs and hence the possibility)Tj-244 -12 TD 0.12 Tc 0 Tw (of Jewish settlement will grow considerably. This proposal has )Tj287 0 TD 0 Tc 0.584 Tw (an enormous advantage and is)Tj-287 -12 TD 0.133 Tc 0 Tw (equivalent in my opinion to the Negev \(if it is put into practice\).")Tj26 -12 TD -0.123 Tc (Ben-Gurion )Tj53 0 TD 0 Tc 2.003 Tw (wrote that when he weighed up the advantages and disadvantages of the)Tj-79 -12 TD 2.523 Tw (Peel Report as against his own plan, he found in general that the former was better. )Tj411 0 TD 0 Tw (He)Tj-411 -12 TD 0.095 Tc (considered that in )Tj84 0 TD 0 Tc 1.713 Tw (two important things "whose value cannot be estimated" the proposals of)Tj-84 -12 TD 0.081 Tc 0 Tw (the Peel Commission excelled. )Tj139 0 TD 0 Tc 2.262 Tw (The first was the inclusion of the Galilee in the Jewish State)Tj-139 -12 TD 0.1 Tc 0 Tw (and the second was the proposal to transfer the Arabs from the valleys. "We were not )Tj388 0 TD 0 Tc 1.038 Tw (able nor)Tj-388 -12 TD 0 Tw (permitted to express such an idea, since we never wanted to )Tj268 0 TD 1.583 Tw (drive out the Arabs. But since the)Tj-268 -12 TD 0.151 Tc 0 Tw (British are diverting part of Palestine which had been promised to us, to the )Tj349 0 TD 0 Tc 2.952 Tw (Arab State, it is)Tj-349 -12 TD 0.191 Tc 0 Tw (only fair that the Arabs in our State be transferred to the Arab area." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf320 3 TD (2)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-298 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.365 Tw (A few months later, in a )Tj117 0 TD 2.239 Tw (further letter which he wrote to his son from London, Ben)Tj278 0 TD (-)Tj-421 -12 TD 1.251 Tw (Gurion displayed more extreme views. Writing about the Negev, Ben-Gurion )Tj357 0 TD 3.576 Tw (suggested that)Tj-357 -12 TD 0.299 Tc 0 Tw (the Arabs might say that "it is )Tj143 0 TD 0 Tc 2.673 Tw (better that the Negev should remain desolate than that the)Tj-143 -12 TD 0.171 Tc 0 Tw (Jews should live in it." Ben-Gurion felt that )Tj200 0 TD 0 Tc 1.995 Tw (a situation where large tracts of land capable of)Tj-200 -12 TD 0 Tw (absorbing large numbers of )Tj124 0 TD 1.837 Tw (Jews were remaining empty, while Jews were being barred from)Tj-124 -12 TD 2.398 Tw (returning to their land under the Arab pretext of insufficient )Tj293 0 TD 2.801 Tw (room for both peoples, was)Tj-293 -12 TD 0 Tw (unacceptable. Ben-Gurion's answer was )Tj178 0 TD 2.27 Tw (simple, "We must expel Arabs and take their place.")Tj-178 -12 TD 2.512 Tw (He explained that the Jews' aspirations were founded on the assumption )Tj351 0 TD 5.733 Tw (that there was)Tj-351 -12 TD 2.056 Tw (sufficient room in Palestine for both Jews and Arabs but "if we have to use force )Tj388 0 TD 2.704 Tw (- not to)Tj-388 -12 TD 0.023 Tc 0 Tw (dispossess the Arabs of the Negev and Transjordan, but to guarantee our right to settle )Tj388 0 TD 0 Tc 2.2 Tw (in those)Tj-388 -12 TD 0.174 Tc 0 Tw (places - then we will have force at our disposal." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf228 3 TD (3)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD (\))Tj-206 -12 TD 0 Tc 1.967 Tw (The above paragraph is quoted \(in English translation\) )Tj260 0 TD 3.104 Tw (exactly as it appears in Ben)Tj135 0 TD (-)Tj-421 -12 TD 0.113 Tc 0 Tw (Gurion's handwritten letter, and also in the typewritten copy, both of which are to be )Tj388 0 TD 0 Tc (found in)Tj-388 -12 TD 0.105 Tc (Ben--Gurion's Archives in Sede Boker. It is )Tj195 0 TD 0 Tc 2.516 Tw (from this text that Shabtai Teveth has quoted in)Tj-195 -12 TD 1.711 Tw (the English version of his book "Ben-Gurion and the Palestinian )Tj301 0 TD 4.46 Tw (Arabs." \()Tj/F4 7 Tf43 3 TD (4)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 2.462 Tw (\) In the Hebrew)Tj-348 -12 TD 0 Tw (version of his book, however, four Hebrew words have been added making it )Tj346 0 TD 1.514 Tw (read, "We do not)Tj-346 -12 TD 1.376 Tw (want and do not need to expel Arabs and take their place." )Tj278 0 TD (\()Tj/F4 7 Tf4 3 TD (5)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 3.289 Tw (\); these same additional four)Tj-286 -12 TD 0.153 Tc 0 Tw (words \(together with the previous two and a half lines\) are in fact )Tj303 0 TD 0 Tc -0.357 Tw (crossed out in Ben-Gurion\325s)Tj-303 -12 TD 2.961 Tw (handwritten letter! In the published edition of this letter,\()Tj/F4 7 Tf277 3 TD (6)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 1.17 Tw (\) )Tj7 0 TD 2.541 Tw (the Editor \(and, according to)Tj-288 -12 TD 0.176 Tc 0 Tw (Shabtai Teveth, with the consent of Ben-Gurion\()Tj/F4 7 Tf221 3 TD (7)Tj/F4 10 Tf4 -3 TD 0.161 Tc (\)\) completely omitted this sentence!)Tj-199 -12 TD 0.019 Tc (From the mid-1990s, a number of historians began to study in depth the )Tj321 0 TD 0 Tc 0.621 Tw ("crossings out" in)Tj-347 -12 TD 0.164 Tc 0 Tw (this letter of Ben-Gurion\325s. In his book "Fabricating Israeli )Tj267 0 TD 0 Tc 3.412 Tw (History", Efraim Karsh, Professor)TjET0.24 w 85.12 181.88 m 228.12 181.88 l S 1 w BT/F4 7 Tf85.5 169 TD (1)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.035 Tc 0 Tw ( / Ben-Gurion to his Children, 7 October 1938, \(BGA\) ; Ben-Gurion, Letters to Paula, \(Tel-Aviv, 1968\), p.247.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (2)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0 Tc ( / Ben-Gurion Memoirs, vol.4, op. cit., pp.330-31.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (3)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 1.268 Tw ( / David Ben-Gurion to Amos Ben-Gurion, 5 October 1937, handwritten letter, \(BGA\) ; typewritten copy )Tj390 0 TD 1.684 Tw (of same)Tj-394 -9 TD 0.067 Tc 0 Tw (letter, p.3, \(BGA\).)Tj/F4 7 Tf0 -7 TD (4)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.024 Tc ( / Shabtai Teveth, Ben-Gurion and the Palestinian Arabs, English ed., \(New York, 1985\), p.189.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (5)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.04 Tc ( / Shabtai Teveth, Ben-Gurion and the Palestinian Arabs, Hebrew ed., \(Jerusalem, 1985\), p.314.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (6)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.039 Tc ( / Ben-Gurion, Letters to Paula, op. cit., p.213.)Tj/F4 7 Tf-4 -7 TD (7)Tj/F4 8 Tf4 -3 TD 0.03 Tc ( / Shabtai Teveth, "Nikayon Kapayim v\325Shichtuv Mismachim", Alpayim, \(Tel-Aviv\), vol.14 \(1997\), p.178.)Tj/F5 7 Tf174 -31 TD 0.25 Tc (\321    30    \321)TjET
