n to this question underwent a change. Edward Norman )Tj349 0 TD 6.518 Tw (found that the)Tj-349 -12 TD 3.397 Tw (enthusiasm of the U.S. Government towards transfer in the )Tj294 0 TD 5.804 Tw (late 1930s had completely)Tj-294 -12 TD 0.135 Tc 0 Tw (evaporated by )Tj68 0 TD 0 Tc 1.897 Tw (1942. Possibly the oil factor of the Middle East which was rapidly becoming)Tj-68 -12 TD -0.046 Tc 0 Tw (more significant during )Tj106 0 TD 0 Tc 1.434 Tw (the course of the Second World War was a reason for this. However,)Tj-106 -12 TD 0.041 Tc 0 Tw (one should mention that throughout this period President Roosevelt would )Tj339 0 TD 0 Tc 6.361 Tw (periodically make)Tj-339 -12 TD 2.688 Tw (statements to his senior officials which were very strongly in favour )Tj332 0 TD 2.032 Tw (of compulsory Arab)Tj-332 -12 TD 0.16 Tc 0 Tw (transfer from Palestine.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 4.829 Tw (Also during the latter part of the )Tj180 0 TD 5.649 Tw (war, former U.S. President Herbert Hoover)Tj-206 -12 TD 0.122 Tc 0 Tw (\(encouraged privately )Tj103 0 TD 0 Tc 1.311 Tw (by leading American Zionists\) began to propose the transfer of Arabs.)Tj-103 -12 TD 0.959 Tw (Towards the end of 1945, in a bout of enthusiasm, he )Tj246 0 TD 2.404 Tw (prepared a statement on this question)Tj-246 -12 TD 0.942 Tw (which was sent to hundreds of American )Tj191 0 TD 2.284 Tw (newspapers. However, to his annoyance very few)Tj-191 -12 TD 0.097 Tc 0 Tw (indeed deigned to publish it, and those who did were mainly the New York Yiddish press.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.202 Tc (On the other side of the Atlantic, )Tj154 0 TD 0 Tc 1.451 Tw (about a year and a half before the end of the Second)Tj-180 -12 TD 2.355 Tw (World War, the British Labour Party commissioned one of its members, )Tj345 0 TD 3.928 Tw (Hugh Dalton, to)Tj-345 -12 TD 0.095 Tc 0 Tw (prepare a document on "Labour and the International Post-War Settlement". )Tj346 0 TD 0 Tc 0.672 Tw (In this document,)Tj-346 -12 TD 1.411 Tw (Dalton included a section on Palestine which included )Tj254 0 TD 2.928 Tw (a paragraph "encouraging" Arabs to)Tj-254 -12 TD 0.318 Tc 0 Tw (leave Palestine. This )Tj99 0 TD 0 Tc 0.55 Tw (document was examined by the various committees and sub-committees)Tj-99 -12 TD 1.674 Tw (of the Party and was finally passed at the Annual Party Conference of 1944 with almost )Tj415 0 TD -0.64 Tc 0 Tw (no)Tj-415 -12 TD 0.079 Tc (opposition. Encouraging Arabs to leave Palestine thus became part of the Party's )Tj365 0 TD 0 Tc 2.305 Tw (policy and it)Tj-365 -12 TD 0.078 Tc 0 Tw (remained as such until after )Tj128 0 TD 0 Tc 1.643 Tw (the general election of 1945, when the Labour Party was elected)Tj-128 -12 TD 0 Tw (to )Tj11 0 TD 1.151 Tw (power in a landslide victory. In commenting on this Labour Party resolution in public, the)Tj-11 -12 TD 2.112 Tw (Zionist leaders said that transfer of Arabs was "inconsistent with )Tj309 0 TD 3.635 Tw (the Zionist programme".)Tj-309 -12 TD 0.039 Tc 0 Tw (However, from a study of their private opinions which are now open to )Tj322 0 TD 0 Tc 1.415 Tw (historians, one can see)Tj-322 -12 TD 0.522 Tc 0 Tw (that they )Tj47 0 TD 0 Tc 2.011 Tw (were quite happy with this transfer proposal! The Jewish Press in Britain and in)Tj-47 -12 TD 0.174 Tc 0 Tw (the U.S. were on the whole favourable to the paragraph advocating Arab transfer.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 3.714 Tw (Following the Labour Party victory )Tj177 0 TD 4.22 Tw (in 1945, Ernest Bevin was appointed Foreign)Tj-203 -12 TD 1.748 Tw (Secretary. The senior civil servants in the Foreign Office who had a long )Tj343 0 TD 4.269 Tw (tradition of anti)Tj78 0 TD (-)Tj-421 -12 TD 2.076 Tw (Zionism, succeeded in persuading Bevin to continue with the policy )Tj324 0 TD 5.255 Tw (of the White Paper,)Tj-324 -12 TD 0.155 Tc 0 Tw (rather than implementing the terms of this Resolution.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 2.766 Tw (The years following the Second World War saw a deterioration in )Tj323 0 TD 4.753 Tw (the situation in)Tj-3