the )Tj281 0 TD 0 Tc 2.476 Tw (British High Commissioner for)Tj-281 -12 TD 0.118 Tc 0 Tw (Palestine, and could thus see the situation at first hand, was in favour of Arab transfer.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.06 Tc (Another interesting phenomenon of the late )Tj199 0 TD 0 Tc 1.211 Tw (1930s and early 1940s was the conviction of)Tj-225 -12 TD 0.106 Tc 0 Tw (some pro-Arabists that the transfer of Arabs from Palestine was the only solution to the )Tj398 0 TD 0 Tc (Arab)Tj23 0 TD (-)Tj-421 -12 TD 2.295 Tw (Jewish conflict. The classic example is that of the pro-Arabist Harry )Tj325 0 TD 3.389 Tw (St. John Philby, who)Tj-325 -12 TD 2.385 Tw (worked for several years on his plan )Tj180 0 TD 3.711 Tw (\(enthusiastically supported by top members of the)Tj-180 -12 TD 3.49 Tw (Zionist leadership\) to transfer almost all the Arabs )Tj253 0 TD 5.285 Tw (from Palestine. Philby had several)Tj-253 -12 TD 1.295 Tw (meetings with King Ibn Saud of Saudi Arabia to try to persuade him to )Tj334 0 TD 2.597 Tw (accept such a plan.)Tj-334 -12 TD 0.961 Tw (Some historians suggest )Tj112 0 TD 2.722 Tw (that at the beginning of the Second World War, the King was in)Tj-112 -12 TD 2.412 Tw (favour of this plan. Even an Arab, Mojli )Tj197 0 TD 2.916 Tw (Amin who was a member of the Arab Defense)Tj-197 -12 TD 0.022 Tc 0 Tw (Committee for Palestine, put forward his own memorandum advocating Arab transfer.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.05 Tc (Towards the end of the 1930s, Iraq completed an irrigation system )Tj298 0 TD 0 Tc 1.692 Tw (but was sadly lacking)Tj-324 -12 TD 2.449 Tw (in population. )Tj70 0 TD 3.654 Tw (It thus became a popular destination for potential Arab transferees from)Tj-70 -12 TD 0.956 Tw (Palestine. Amongst those proposing Iraq, was Ben-Gurion, who in )Tj304 0 TD 2.023 Tw (1938-39 often put forward)Tj-304 -12 TD 1.597 Tw (the idea of Arab transfer to that country. Support )Tj234 0 TD 2.201 Tw (for this plan of Ben-Gurion's came from,)Tj-234 -12 TD 0.142 Tc 0 Tw (amongst others, 