nn in his letters and )Tj130 0 TD 0 Tc 2.123 Tw (meetings of that period displayed a similar enthusiasm on this)Tj-130 -12 TD 0.049 Tc 0 Tw (subject. At the 20th Zionist Congress which took )Tj219 0 TD 0 Tc 1.8 Tw (place about a month after the publication of)Tj-219 -12 TD 3.644 Tw (this Report, many of the participants spoke in favour of )Tj284 0 TD 6.051 Tw (transfer, although when the)Tj-284 -12 TD 2.68 Tw ("official" minutes were )Tj111 0 TD 2.401 Tw (published, many of their comments on transfer were omitted! Berl)Tj-111 -12 TD 0.036 Tc 0 Tw (Katznelson, who was known as the "conscience" of the )Tj245 0 TD 0 Tc 0.963 Tw (Jewish Labour Party, spoke up strongly)Tj-245 -12 TD 0.045 Tc 0 Tw (in favour of transfer at a meeting of )Tj161 0 TD 0 Tc 2.748 Tw (the "Council of World Unity" \(the amalgamated Zionist)Tj-161 -12 TD 0.365 Tc 0 Tw (Socialist parties\) held a )Tj114 0 TD 0 Tc 1.367 Tw (few weeks before the 20th Zionist Congress. In contrast, Jabotinsky,)Tj-114 -12 TD 0.114 Tc 0 Tw (leader of the Revisionist movement )Tj163 0 TD 0 Tc 1.729 Tw (came out very strongly against transfer. This in fact had)Tj-163 -12 TD 0 Tw (been his stand for decades.)Tj26 -12 TD 1.583 Tw (When debated in )Tj83 0 TD 3.543 Tw (the British Parliament, several members of Parliament, who were)Tj-109 -12 TD 5.721 Tw (members of the pro-Arab lobby, came out in favour of, and even )Tj356 0 TD 9.151 Tw (exceeded, the)Tj/F5 7 Tf-178 -32 TD 0.25 Tc 0 Tw (\321    12    \321)TjET
