BT/F2 7 Tf181.5 781 TD 0.023 Tc 0 Tw (Chaim SIMONS : Proposals to Transfer Arabs from Palestine)Tj-10 -10 TD -0.18 Tc (\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321\321)Tj/F3 12 Tf45 -122 TD 0 Tc (A HISTORICAL OVERVIEW)Tj/F4 10 Tf-105 -61 TD 1.105 Tw (The era of "Modern Zionism" can )Tj156 0 TD 2.301 Tw (be said to have begun towards the end of the 19th)Tj-182 -12 TD 0.279 Tc 0 Tw (century with the "Hovevei Zion", the "First Aliyah", and Theodor Herzl.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc (In one )Tj30 0 TD 2.827 Tw (of the first entries in his private diary dated June 1895, \(even before he had)Tj-56 -12 TD 0.129 Tc 0 Tw (decided on the final location )Tj132 0 TD 0 Tc 1.91 Tw (of the Jewish State\), Herzl wrote that it would be necessary to)Tj-132 -12 TD 0.102 Tc 0 Tw (remove the non-Jews from such a state. Herzl apparently realised that it would not )Tj377 0 TD 0 Tc (be prudent)Tj-377 -12 TD 0.086 Tc (to publicise such an idea, since there is not a hint of it )Tj243 0 TD 0 Tc 2.125 Tw (in his famous book "The Jewish State",)Tj-243 -12 TD 0.115 Tc 0 Tw (which was published just a few months later.)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc (In contrast, )Tj52 0 TD 1.838 Tw (Nachman Syrkin, who was one of the founders of "Socialist Zionism", had)Tj-78 -12 TD 1.243 Tw (no inhibitions about making public the )Tj182 0 TD 2.912 Tw (possibility of transfer of Arabs from Palestine, and)Tj-182 -12 TD 0.082 Tc 0 Tw (such a proposal appears in his booklet published in 1898.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.156 Tc (In the same year, Herzl visited Palestine and saw the country at first hand. A )Tj354 0 TD 0 Tc 2.5 Tw (few years)Tj-380 -12 TD 0.204 Tc 0 Tw (later in his unpublished "Draft Charter" for Palestine he wrote that the Jews would have )Tj409 0 TD 0.709 Tc (the)Tj-409 -12 TD 0 Tc 3.612 Tw (right to transfer Arabs to other parts of the Ottoman Empire. Another )Tj353 0 TD 4.521 Tw (person to visit)Tj-353 -12 TD 0.237 Tc 0 Tw (Palestine at that period was the Anglo-Jewish writer Israel Zangwill, who, after a )Tj380 0 TD 0 Tc 2.5 Tw (few years)Tj-380 -12 TD 0.069 Tc 0 Tw (reflection, proposed such transfer in lectures which he )Tj246 0 TD 0 Tc 1.996 Tw (gave in the U.S.A. and Britain in 1904)Tj-246 -12 TD -0.054 Tc 0 Tw (and 1905. One should note that the public pronouncements )Tj261 0 TD 0 Tc 1.039 Tw (on this question by both Syrkin and)Tj-261 -12 TD 0.032 Tc 0 Tw (Zangwill did not give rise to any adverse comments.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.227 Tc (At this period, the Zionist )Tj123 0 TD 0 Tc 1.44 Tw (movement was still in its infancy and proposals for transfer)Tj-149 -12 TD 1.812 Tw (were made by only a )Tj104 0 TD 4.862 Tw (few individuals, particularly Zangwill. Following the rejection of)Tj-104 -12 TD 0.146 Tc 0 Tw (Uganda as the location )Tj107 0 TD 0 Tc 1.788 Tw (for a Jewish Homeland in 1905, Zangwill left the Zionist movement,)Tj-107 -12 TD 1.668 Tw (and it seems that )Tj84 0 TD 1.765 Tw (no further proposals for Arab transfer were put forward for a number of)Tj-84 -12 TD 0.327 Tc 0 Tw (years.)Tj26 -12 TD 0.174 Tc (It was in the early 1910s that two leading Zionists, )Tj233 0 TD 0 Tc 0.638 Tw (Arthur Ruppin and Leo Motzkin put)Tj-259 -12 TD 1.783 Tw (forward transfer proposals, the former in a private )Tj240 0 TD 2.845 Tw (letter and the latter in the course of a)Tj-240 -12 TD 0.708 Tw (lecture to a Conference )Tj107 0 TD 1.93 Tw (of German Zionists which was subsequently published in a German)Tj-107 -12 TD 0.093 Tc 0 Tw (Jewish newspaper. However, the main proposer of transfer at this period )Tj332 0 TD 0 Tc 2.84 Tw (was Zangwill, who,)Tj-332 -12 TD 0.105 Tc 0 Tw (after he had returned to the Zionist fold, wrote a number of articles and delivered )Tj372 0 TD 0 Tc (a number of)Tj-372 -12 TD (lectures on this subject.)Tj26 -12 TD 1.287 Tw (At the end of 1918, following one of Zangwill's )Tj221 0 TD 2.639 Tw (articles, a public condemnation of his)Tj-247 -12 TD 0.052 Tc 0 Tw (proposals by several prominent Anglo-Jews, appeared for the )Tj278 0 TD 0 Tc 3.74 Tw (first time in the British-Jewish)Tj-278 -12 TD 0.102 Tc 0 Tw (press. One should remember, however, that this was the period of the )Tj318 0 TD 0 Tc 3.827 Tw (Balfour Declaration. A)Tj-318 -12 TD 0.395 Tw (number of prominent Anglo-Jews from families )Tj216 0 TD 4.014 Tw (who were well-established in Britain, were)Tj-216 -12 TD 1.416 Tw (vigorously opposed to the establishment of a )Tj211 0 TD 3.049 Tw (Jewish National Home in Palestine and as a)Tj-211 -12 TD 2.218 Tw (result of their efforts, the final text of the )Tj201 0 TD 3.489 Tw (Balfour Declaration was less favourable to the)Tj-201 -12 TD 0.154 Tc 0 Tw (Zionist )Tj35 0 TD 0 Tc 2.236 Tw (aspirations. The Anglo-Jews publicly opposing Zangwill's transfer proposals largely)Tj-35 -12 TD 2.646 Tw (came from these well-established families. To their great credit, the )Tj325 0 TD 1.777 Tw (press did not prevent)Tj-325 -12 TD 2.134 Tw (Zangwill from using their columns to propagate his ideas on Arab )Tj319 0 TD 3.691 Tw (transfer - "freedom of)Tj-319 -12 TD 0.176 Tc 0 Tw (expression" was sacred at that period!)Tj26 -12 TD 0 Tc 4.228 Tw (Following the termination )Tj131 0 TD 4.889 Tw (of the First World War, Fridtjof Nansen, proposed a)Tj-157 -12 TD 0.566 Tw (compulsory transfer of population between Greece )Tj231 0 TD 2.604 Tw (and Turkey involving nearly two million)Tj-231 -12 TD 0.036 Tc 0 Tw (people and this proposal was subsequently implemented by the League of Nations. )Tj374 0 TD 0 Tc (The success)Tj/F5 7 Tf-196 -42 TD 0.25 Tc (\321    11    \321)TjET
